{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T06:51:44.017372", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    # Action constants (assuming these are globally defined or otherwise accessible)\n    # DOWN = 0\n    # UP = 1\n    # LEFT = 2\n    # RIGHT = 3\n    # USE = 4\n\n    # Direction constants (matching CraftState internal values)\n    # 0: East, 1: South, 2: West, 3: North\n    # EAST = 0\n    # SOUTH = 1\n    # WEST = 2\n    # NORTH = 3\n\n    # Delta Row (DR) and Delta Column (DC) for each direction\n    # Maps direction to (dr, dc) based on CraftState.dir\n    # DR = [0, 1, 0, -1] # Index: 0=EAST, 1=SOUTH, 2=WEST, 3=NORTH\n    # DC = [1, 0, -1, 0] # Index: 0=EAST, 1=SOUTH, 2=WEST, 3=NORTH\n\n    # Mapping of movement action to (delta_row, delta_col, new_direction)\n    # This reflects how CraftState.step handles movement actions and updates direction\n    # ACTION_MOVE_INFO = {\n    #     DOWN: (1, 0, SOUTH),\n    #     UP: (-1, 0, NORTH),\n    #     LEFT: (0, -1, WEST),\n    #     RIGHT: (0, 1, EAST),\n    # }\n\n    # Re-defining constants here if they are not globally available.\n    # For a real system, these would ideally be module-level constants.\n    # Given the existing global imports, it's highly probable these are also global.\n    # However, to strictly adhere to \"only return code that will fit in that function\",\n    # one might put them here. For efficiency and typical Python practice, assuming globals.\n    # Assuming the following constants are available in the global scope:\n    # DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT, USE (from action_specs)\n    # EAST, SOUTH, WEST, NORTH (internal CraftState direction values)\n    # DR, DC (deltas for rows/cols based on direction)\n    # ACTION_MOVE_INFO (mapping action to (dr, dc, new_dir))\n\n    # To make this code self-contained if constants are truly not global:\n    # import collections\n    # DOWN = 0; UP = 1; LEFT = 2; RIGHT = 3; USE = 4\n    # EAST = 0; SOUTH = 1; WEST = 2; NORTH = 3\n    # DR = [0, 1, 0, -1]; DC = [1, 0, -1, 0]\n    # ACTION_MOVE_INFO = {DOWN: (1, 0, SOUTH), UP: (-1, 0, NORTH), LEFT: (0, -1, WEST), RIGHT: (0, 1, EAST)}\n    # (Leaving these commented out as per \"Do not imports\" and assuming globals)\n\n    # Get the current state from the CraftLab environment\n    current_state = env._current_state\n    \n    # 1. Check if the primitive is already in inventory\n    if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n        return []\n\n    # 2. Find all locations of the primitive on the grid\n    primitive_locations = []\n    grid_rows, grid_cols, _ = current_state.grid.shape\n    for r in range(grid_rows):\n        for c in range(grid_cols):\n            if current_state.grid[r, c, primitive] > 0:\n                primitive_locations.append((r, c))\n\n    # If the primitive is not found on the map, it cannot be collected\n    if not primitive_locations:\n        return []\n\n    # 3. Perform a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n    #    to a position and orientation from which the primitive can be USED.\n    # BFS state: (current_row, current_col, current_direction, path_actions)\n    q = collections.deque([(current_state.pos[0], current_state.pos[1], current_state.dir, [])])\n    \n    # Visited set to store (row, col, direction) tuples to avoid cycles and redundant searches\n    visited = {(current_state.pos[0], current_state.pos[1], current_state.dir)}\n\n    best_path_to_use = None\n\n    while q:\n        r, c, d, path_actions = q.popleft()\n\n        # Check if the cell directly in front of the agent contains the primitive\n        # If so, this path leads to a state where USE can collect the primitive\n        r_front = r + DR[d]\n        c_front = c + DC[d]\n\n        # Ensure r_front, c_front are within bounds before checking primitive_locations\n        if (0 <= r_front < grid_rows and 0 <= c_front < grid_cols and\n            (r_front, c_front) in primitive_locations):\n            best_path_to_use = path_actions + [USE] # Add USE action at the end\n            break # Found the shortest path, no need to continue BFS\n\n        # Explore possible movement actions\n        for action in [DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT]:\n            dr, dc, new_d = ACTION_MOVE_INFO[action]\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n\n            # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries\n            if 0 <= nr < grid_rows and 0 <= nc < grid_cols:\n                # Check if this (position, direction) state has been visited\n                if (nr, nc, new_d) not in visited:\n                    visited.add((nr, nc, new_d))\n                    q.append((nr, nc, new_d, path_actions + [action]))\n\n    # If no path was found, return an empty list\n    if best_path_to_use is None:\n        return []\n    \n    return best_path_to_use", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T06:52:47.949387", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  from collections import deque\n\n  actions = []\n  \n  # Get current state information from the environment\n  obs = env.observations()\n  grid = obs['features_dict']['features_global']\n  # Ensure position is int tuple. CraftState.pos is tuple(int, int)\n  # The features_dict['pos'] might be normalized or float, so convert to int tuple.\n  current_pos = tuple(obs['features_dict']['pos'].astype(int)) \n  \n  world = env.world\n  # non_grabbable_indices typically include obstacles like water, stone walls, workshops.\n  non_grabbable_indices = world.non_grabbable_indices\n  \n  W, H, K = grid.shape\n\n  # 1. Determine traversable cells more efficiently using NumPy operations.\n  # A cell is NOT traversable if it contains any non-grabbable item (obstacle).\n  if non_grabbable_indices:\n      non_grabbable_list = list(non_grabbable_indices)\n      # Select slices for non-grabbable kinds, check for presence (>0), and then check if ANY are present along the kind axis (axis=2)\n      obstacles_present = np.any(grid[:, :, non_grabbable_list] > 0, axis=2)\n      # Invert the mask: where obstacles are present is not traversable, where not present is traversable\n      traversable_mask = ~obstacles_present\n  else:\n      # If there are no non-grabbable indices, all cells are traversable.\n      traversable_mask = np.ones((W, H), dtype=bool)\n  \n  # Ensure the agent's current position is marked as traversable.\n  if not traversable_mask[current_pos[0], current_pos[1]]:\n      return [] # Agent starts on an untraversable cell, no path possible.\n\n  # Action constants (from problem description context)\n  # These are assumed to be accessible from the surrounding scope.\n  # DOWN = 0\n  # UP = 1\n  # LEFT = 2\n  # RIGHT = 3\n  # USE = 4\n\n  MOVES = {\n      UP: (0, -1),\n      DOWN: (0, 1),\n      LEFT: (-1, 0),\n      RIGHT: (1, 0),\n  }\n\n  # Helper function to check if a position is adjacent to the primitive\n  # This reflects the 3x3 neighborhood effect of the USE action in CraftState.\n  def _is_adjacent_to_primitive(pos_to_check, grid_data, primitive_idx, grid_W, grid_H):\n      px, py = pos_to_check\n      # Iterate over 3x3 neighborhood, including the center cell\n      for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              nx, ny = px + dx, py + dy\n              # Check bounds and if the cell contains the primitive\n              if 0 <= nx < grid_W and 0 <= ny < grid_H and grid_data[nx, ny, primitive_idx] > 0:\n                  return True\n      return False\n\n  # 2. Perform BFS to find the shortest path to any location from which the primitive can be collected.\n  # The target of BFS is now a cell (x,y) from which _is_adjacent_to_primitive is true.\n  q = deque([(current_pos, [])]) # (current_pos, path_so_far_actions)\n  visited = {current_pos}\n  \n  path_to_adjacent_pos = []\n\n  while q:\n      (curr_x, curr_y), actions_so_far = q.popleft()\n      curr_pos_tuple = (curr_x, curr_y)\n\n      # Check if the current position is adjacent to the target primitive.\n      # If so, we've found a path to a location from which a USE action can collect the primitive.\n      if _is_adjacent_to_primitive(curr_pos_tuple, grid, primitive, W, H):\n          path_to_adjacent_pos = actions_so_far\n          break # Found the shortest path to an adjacent location\n\n      # Explore neighbors\n      for action, (dx, dy) in MOVES.items():\n          next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # Check bounds, traversability, and if already visited\n          if (0 <= next_x < W and 0 <= next_y < H and\n              traversable_mask[next_x, next_y] and\n              next_pos not in visited):\n              \n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              q.append((next_pos, actions_so_far + [action]))\n  \n  # If no path was found to an adjacent cell, and the agent is not already\n  # at such a cell, return an empty list.\n  if not path_to_adjacent_pos and not _is_adjacent_to_primitive(current_pos, grid, primitive, W, H):\n      return [] \n  \n  # 3. Append the USE action after the movement path.\n  # If path_to_adjacent_pos is empty, it implies the agent is already at a position\n  # from which it can collect the primitive (i.e., it's adjacent or on it).\n  actions.extend(path_to_adjacent_pos)\n  actions.append(USE)\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T06:52:48.921703", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Action constants (derived from CraftLab.action_specs)\n  DOWN = 0\n  UP = 1\n  LEFT = 2\n  RIGHT = 3\n  USE = 4\n\n  # Relative movements for each action\n  MOVES = {\n      UP: (0, -1),   # (dr, dc) for (row_change, col_change)\n      DOWN: (0, 1),\n      LEFT: (-1, 0),\n      RIGHT: (1, 0),\n  }\n\n  # Retrieve current state information from the environment\n  obs = env.observations()\n  grid = obs['features_dict']['features_global']\n  # Agent's position from observation features, converted to integer tuple (row, col).\n  current_pos = tuple(obs['features_dict']['pos'].astype(int)) \n  \n  world = env.world\n  # Indices of entities that cannot be picked up or walked through (obstacles).\n  non_grabbable_indices = world.non_grabbable_indices\n  \n  H, W, _ = grid.shape # Grid dimensions (Height, Width, Kinds)\n\n  # 1. Determine traversable cells: a cell is traversable if it does not contain any non-grabbable item.\n  # Initialize all cells as traversable.\n  traversable_mask = np.ones((H, W), dtype=bool) \n  if non_grabbable_indices:\n      # Convert set of non-grabbable indices to a list/array for efficient NumPy slicing.\n      non_grabbable_array = np.array(list(non_grabbable_indices))\n      # Identify cells containing any non-grabbable obstacle.\n      # np.any along axis=2 checks if any of the specified 'kinds' are present in a cell.\n      obstacles_present = np.any(grid[:, :, non_grabbable_array] > 0, axis=2)\n      # Invert the mask: where obstacles are present, it's NOT traversable.\n      traversable_mask = ~obstacles_present\n  \n  # Edge case: If the agent starts on an untraversable cell, no path is possible.\n  if not traversable_mask[current_pos[0], current_pos[1]]:\n      return []\n\n  # 2. Perform Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path to any location\n  #    containing the target primitive.\n  # The queue stores tuples: (current_position_tuple, list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_this_position).\n  queue = deque([(current_pos, [])])\n  # Keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles and redundant checks.\n  visited = {current_pos} \n  \n  path_to_primitive_actions = [] # This list will store the movement actions to the primitive.\n\n  while queue:\n      (r, c), actions_so_far = queue.popleft() # Dequeue the current position and its path\n\n      # Check if the current cell contains the target primitive.\n      if grid[r, c, primitive] > 0:\n          path_to_primitive_actions = actions_so_far\n          break # Shortest path found, exit BFS.\n\n      # Explore all four cardinal neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT)\n      for action, (dr, dc) in MOVES.items():\n          next_r, next_c = r + dr, c + dc\n          next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n\n          # Validate the next position: within grid bounds, traversable, and not yet visited.\n          if (0 <= next_r < H and 0 <= next_c < W and\n              traversable_mask[next_r, next_c] and\n              next_pos not in visited):\n              \n              visited.add(next_pos) # Mark as visited\n              # Enqueue the new position with the updated path (append the new action).\n              queue.append((next_pos, actions_so_far + [action]))\n  \n  # 3. Construct the final sequence of actions.\n  # If `path_to_primitive_actions` is empty, it means either:\n  #   a) The agent started on the primitive's cell (BFS loop broke immediately).\n  #   b) The primitive is unreachable via any traversable path.\n  # We must distinguish between these two cases for the return value.\n  if not path_to_primitive_actions and not grid[current_pos[0], current_pos[1], primitive] > 0:\n      return [] # Primitive is unreachable from the current position.\n\n  # Append the 'USE' action after all movement actions.\n  # If `path_to_primitive_actions` is empty, it correctly results in just `[USE]`.\n  return path_to_primitive_actions + [USE]", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T06:54:41.757509", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    # Get action mappings from the environment dynamically, as they are not global constants here\n    action_map = env.action_specs()\n    DOWN_ACTION = action_map[\"DOWN\"]\n    UP_ACTION = action_map[\"UP\"]\n    LEFT_ACTION = action_map[\"LEFT\"]\n    RIGHT_ACTION = action_map[\"RIGHT\"]\n    USE_ACTION = action_map[\"USE\"]\n\n    # Define the change in (x, y) coordinates for each movement action\n    ACTIONS_DELTA = {\n        UP_ACTION: (0, -1),\n        DOWN_ACTION: (0, 1),\n        LEFT_ACTION: (-1, 0),\n        RIGHT_ACTION: (1, 0),\n    }\n\n    # Map the agent's internal direction index (0=UP, 1=DOWN, 2=LEFT, 3=RIGHT) to a (dx, dy) delta.\n    # This is used to determine the cell directly in front of the agent.\n    DIR_TO_DELTA = {\n        0: (0, -1), # UP (y-decreases)\n        1: (0, 1),  # DOWN (y-increases)\n        2: (-1, 0), # LEFT (x-decreases)\n        3: (1, 0),  # RIGHT (x-increases)\n    }\n\n    # Map each movement action to the resulting agent direction.\n    # In CraftWorld, the agent's direction updates to match the last movement.\n    ACTION_TO_DIR_MAP = {\n        UP_ACTION: 0,\n        DOWN_ACTION: 1,\n        LEFT_ACTION: 2,\n        RIGHT_ACTION: 3,\n    }\n\n    # Access the current state of the environment directly\n    current_state = env._current_state\n\n    # 1. Check if the primitive is already in the agent's inventory\n    if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n        return [] # Already collected, no actions needed\n\n    grid = current_state.grid\n    WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n\n    # BFS for pathfinding\n    # A state in the BFS is represented as (x, y, direction_idx),\n    # storing the agent's current position and its facing direction.\n    # The queue stores tuples of ((x, y, dir), list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_this_state).\n    initial_pos_x, initial_pos_y = current_state.pos\n    initial_dir = current_state.dir\n\n    q = deque([((initial_pos_x, initial_pos_y, initial_dir), [])])\n    # Keep track of visited states to avoid cycles and redundant paths\n    visited = set([(initial_pos_x, initial_pos_y, initial_dir)])\n\n    while q:\n        (cx, cy, c_dir), path = q.popleft()\n\n        # Check if the primitive can be collected from the current (position, direction)\n        # Calculate the coordinates of the cell directly in front of the agent\n        dx_front, dy_front = DIR_TO_DELTA[c_dir]\n        target_x, target_y = cx + dx_front, cy + dy_front\n\n        # Ensure the target cell is within grid boundaries\n        if 0 <= target_x < WIDTH and 0 <= target_y < HEIGHT:\n            # Check if the target cell contains the desired primitive\n            if grid[target_x, target_y, primitive] == 1:\n                # If yes, we found a path. Append the USE action and return the full sequence.\n                return path + [USE_ACTION]\n\n        # Explore possible movement actions from the current state\n        # Each movement action updates both the agent's position and its facing direction.\n        for action in [UP_ACTION, DOWN_ACTION, LEFT_ACTION, RIGHT_ACTION]:\n            dx, dy = ACTIONS_DELTA[action]\n            nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy  # New position after the move\n            n_dir = ACTION_TO_DIR_MAP[action] # New direction after the move (matches move direction)\n\n            # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries\n            # (Assuming no other obstacles beyond grid walls for simplicity in this BFS)\n            if 0 <= nx < WIDTH and 0 <= ny < HEIGHT:\n                # If this new state (position and direction) has not been visited, add it to the queue\n                if (nx, ny, n_dir) not in visited:\n                    visited.add((nx, ny, n_dir))\n                    q.append(((nx, ny, n_dir), path + [action]))\n\n    # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path was found, it means the primitive\n    # is unreachable from the current state.\n    return []", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T06:54:41.832612", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    actions = []\n    \n    # Get the integer ID for the primitive\n    primitive_id = env.world.cookbook.index.index(primitive)\n\n    # Create a deep copy of the current environment state for simulation\n    # Using type(obj) to get the class ensures it works even if CraftState\n    # is renamed or wrapped, as long as the constructor signature is consistent.\n    current_actual_state = env._current_state\n    simulated_state_initial = type(current_actual_state)(\n        current_actual_state.scenario,\n        current_actual_state.grid.copy(),        # Deep copy the grid\n        current_actual_state.pos,\n        current_actual_state.dir,\n        current_actual_state.inventory.copy()    # Deep copy the inventory\n    )\n\n    WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = simulated_state_initial.grid.shape\n\n    # Define actions using env_factory constants (already imported)\n    ACTION_UP = env_factory.ACTIONS['UP']\n    ACTION_DOWN = env_factory.ACTIONS['DOWN']\n    ACTION_LEFT = env_factory.ACTIONS['LEFT']\n    ACTION_RIGHT = env_factory.ACTIONS['RIGHT']\n    ACTION_USE = env_factory.ACTIONS['USE']\n\n    # Mapping of (dx, dy) from agent to target to desired direction (0=N, 1=E, 2=S, 3=W)\n    # Used to determine if the agent is facing the target for the USE action.\n    DELTAS_TO_DIR = {\n        (0, -1): 0, # Up / North\n        (1, 0): 1,  # Right / East\n        (0, 1): 2,  # Down / South\n        (-1, 0): 3  # Left / West\n    }\n\n    # BFS Queue: stores tuples of (simulated_CraftState, list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state)\n    q = [(simulated_state_initial, [])]\n    \n    # Visited states: set of (pos_x, pos_y, dir, primitive_inventory_count) to avoid cycles and redundant exploration.\n    # The primitive_inventory_count is crucial for states where the item might have been picked up.\n    visited_states = set([ (simulated_state_initial.pos[0], \n                            simulated_state_initial.pos[1], \n                            simulated_state_initial.dir, \n                            simulated_state_initial.inventory[primitive_id]) ])\n\n    best_path = None\n    \n    # Maximum steps for BFS to prevent infinite loops in complex scenarios.\n    # A heuristic: total possible (pos, dir) states multiplied by a small factor\n    # to allow for some detours or complex maneuvers.\n    MAX_BFS_STEPS = WIDTH * HEIGHT * 4 * 2 # 4 directions, factor of 2 for safety\n\n    while q:\n        current_sim_state, current_path = q.pop(0)\n\n        # Check if the primitive is already in inventory (goal achieved)\n        if current_sim_state.inventory[primitive_id] > 0:\n            best_path = current_path\n            break # Found a path to collect, shortest path first due to BFS\n\n        # Prevent excessively long paths\n        if len(current_path) >= MAX_BFS_STEPS:\n            continue # Don't explore further from this path, consider it uncollectible via this route\n\n        # Find the target primitive's location in the current simulated grid.\n        # It's important to re-check the grid in case it changed (e.g., if another agent picked it up,\n        # though this simulation is single-agent).\n        # We also ensure the target isn't the agent's current position if that would prevent picking up.\n        current_primitive_xy = None\n        for x in range(WIDTH):\n            for y in range(HEIGHT):\n                if current_sim_state.grid[x, y, primitive_id] > 0 and (x, y) != current_sim_state.pos:\n                    current_primitive_xy = (x, y)\n                    break\n            if current_primitive_xy:\n                break\n        \n        # If the primitive is no longer on the grid, we can't collect it from here in this path branch.\n        if current_primitive_xy:\n            # Calculate vector from agent to primitive\n            dx_to_target = current_primitive_xy[0] - current_sim_state.pos[0]\n            dy_to_target = current_primitive_xy[1] - current_sim_state.pos[1]\n            \n            # Check if agent is adjacent (cardinal directions only for simplicity of USE)\n            is_adjacent_cardinal = (abs(dx_to_target) == 1 and dy_to_target == 0) or \\\n                                   (abs(dy_to_target) == 1 and dx_to_target == 0)\n\n            if is_adjacent_cardinal:\n                # Check if agent is facing the primitive\n                desired_dir_tuple = (dx_to_target, dy_to_target)\n                if desired_dir_tuple in DELTAS_TO_DIR:\n                    desired_dir = DELTAS_TO_DIR[desired_dir_tuple]\n                    \n                    if current_sim_state.dir == desired_dir:\n                        # Agent is adjacent and facing the primitive, try USE action\n                        next_action = ACTION_USE\n                        \n                        # Simulate the USE action\n                        _, new_state_after_use = current_sim_state.step(next_action)\n                        new_path = current_path + [next_action]\n                        \n                        # Add to queue if the resulting state (pos, dir, inventory_count) hasn't been visited\n                        visited_key_after_use = (new_state_after_use.pos[0], \n                                                new_state_after_use.pos[1], \n                                                new_state_after_use.dir,\n                                                new_state_after_use.inventory[primitive_id])\n                        if visited_key_after_use not in visited_states:\n                            visited_states.add(visited_key_after_use)\n                            q.append((new_state_after_use, new_path))\n                        # Note: We continue exploring movement actions from `current_sim_state` below\n                        # in case `USE` didn't succeed or a different sequence is needed.\n                        # For a shortest path BFS, if `USE` leads to goal, it will be the first path found.\n\n        # Explore movement actions (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT)\n        for action_val in [ACTION_UP, ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_LEFT, ACTION_RIGHT]:\n            # Simulate the action\n            _, next_sim_state = current_sim_state.step(action_val)\n            next_path = current_path + [action_val]\n\n            # Check if this new state has been visited.\n            # The inventory count of the primitive does not change from movement actions,\n            # but it's included for consistency in the visited key.\n            visited_key_move = (next_sim_state.pos[0], \n                                next_sim_state.pos[1], \n                                next_sim_state.dir,\n                                next_sim_state.inventory[primitive_id]) \n            \n            if visited_key_move not in visited_states:\n                visited_states.add(visited_key_move)\n                q.append((next_sim_state, next_path))\n\n    if best_path is None:\n        return [] # No path found to collect the item within the given limits\n    else:\n        return best_path", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T06:55:44.474420", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import collections\n\n  # Action constants (numerical values from CraftLab's action_specs)\n  ACTION_DOWN = 0\n  ACTION_UP = 1\n  ACTION_LEFT = 2\n  ACTION_RIGHT = 3\n  ACTION_USE = 4\n\n  # Defines movement for each action: (dx, dy, resulting_facing_direction_index)\n  # The direction indices (0:UP, 1:RIGHT, 2:DOWN, 3:LEFT) are assumed consistent\n  # with how the agent's internal direction changes after movement.\n  MOVE_ACTIONS_PROPERTIES = {\n      ACTION_UP: (0, -1, 0),    # Move UP: change Y by -1, new facing_dir is 0 (UP)\n      ACTION_RIGHT: (1, 0, 1),  # Move RIGHT: change X by +1, new facing_dir is 1 (RIGHT)\n      ACTION_DOWN: (0, 1, 2),   # Move DOWN: change Y by +1, new facing_dir is 2 (DOWN)\n      ACTION_LEFT: (-1, 0, 3),  # Move LEFT: change X by -1, new facing_dir is 3 (LEFT)\n  }\n\n  # 1. Pre-checks: If the primitive is not a grabbable item, it cannot be \"collected\".\n  if primitive not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # Get current state information from the environment's internal state\n  initial_state = env._current_state\n  start_x, start_y = initial_state.pos\n  start_dir = initial_state.dir # Agent's initial facing direction (0, 1, 2, or 3)\n  grid = initial_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Get the set of indices for non-grabbable entities (obstacles)\n  non_grabbable_kinds = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Helper function to check if a grid cell is within bounds and not occupied by an obstacle.\n  def is_walkable(x, y):\n    if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n      return False # Out of bounds\n    \n    # Check if the cell is occupied by any non-grabbable item (which acts as an obstacle).\n    for k_idx in non_grabbable_kinds:\n      if grid[x, y, k_idx] == 1: # Assuming 1 indicates presence of the kind\n        return False\n    return True\n\n  # 2. Pre-compute all (agent_x, agent_y, agent_direction) states from which the primitive\n  # can be collected by performing an ACTION_USE.\n  collectable_states = set()\n\n  # Iterate through all cells in the grid to find instances of the target primitive.\n  for px in range(grid_width):\n    for py in range(grid_height):\n      if grid[px, py, primitive] == 1:\n        # This cell (px, py) contains the primitive.\n        # Now, find all possible agent positions (ax, ay) and agent directions (adir)\n        # such that the agent at (ax, ay) facing adir would point to (px, py).\n        \n        # Iterate over all possible movement actions and their properties\n        for action_val, (dx, dy, agent_dir) in MOVE_ACTIONS_PROPERTIES.items():\n          # If an agent at (ax, ay) moves by (dx, dy) to (px, py),\n          # then its current position (ax, ay) must be (px - dx, py - dy).\n          ax, ay = px - dx, py - dy\n\n          # If this agent position is walkable, add the full state to collectable_states.\n          if is_walkable(ax, ay):\n            collectable_states.add((ax, ay, agent_dir))\n\n  # If no collectable primitive instances are found on the grid, or no reachable collection points,\n  # return an empty path.\n  if not collectable_states:\n      return []\n\n  # 3. Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest sequence of actions.\n  # Queue stores tuples: (current_x, current_y, current_direction, list_of_actions_taken)\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_x, start_y, start_dir, [])])\n\n  # Visited set to avoid redundant exploration and cycles. A state is defined by\n  # (x, y, direction) because the agent's direction affects what it can interact with (USE action).\n  visited = set([(start_x, start_y, start_dir)])\n\n  while queue:\n    curr_x, curr_y, curr_dir, path_actions = queue.popleft()\n\n    # Check if the current state is one from which the primitive can be collected.\n    if (curr_x, curr_y, curr_dir) in collectable_states:\n      return path_actions + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # Explore possible next movement actions.\n    for action, (move_dx, move_dy, next_dir) in MOVE_ACTIONS_PROPERTIES.items():\n      next_x, next_y = curr_x + move_dx, curr_y + move_dy\n\n      # If the next cell is walkable and this (position, direction) state hasn't been visited,\n      # add it to the queue for further exploration.\n      if is_walkable(next_x, next_y) and (next_x, next_y, next_dir) not in visited:\n        visited.add((next_x, next_y, next_dir))\n        queue.append((next_x, next_y, next_dir, path_actions + [action]))\n\n  # If the queue becomes empty and no path to collect the primitive was found.\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T06:55:45.484845", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import collections\n\n  # Constants for actions and directions, consistent with CraftWorld/CraftLab\n  ACTION_DOWN = 0\n  ACTION_UP = 1\n  ACTION_LEFT = 2\n  ACTION_RIGHT = 3\n  ACTION_USE = 4\n\n  ACTION_TO_DIR = {\n      ACTION_UP: 0,\n      ACTION_RIGHT: 1,\n      ACTION_DOWN: 2,\n      ACTION_LEFT: 3\n  }\n\n  DIR_VEC = {\n      0: (0, -1),  # UP: (dx, dy) - decreasing y\n      1: (1, 0),   # RIGHT: increasing x\n      2: (0, 1),   # DOWN: increasing y\n      3: (-1, 0)   # LEFT: decreasing x\n  }\n\n  # 1. Initial check: If the primitive is already in the inventory, no actions are needed.\n  if env._current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # 2. Pre-check: If the primitive is not a grabbable item, it cannot be \"collected\".\n  if primitive not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # Get current state information\n  initial_state = env._current_state\n  start_x, start_y = initial_state.pos\n  start_dir = initial_state.dir # Agent's initial facing direction (0, 1, 2, or 3)\n  grid = initial_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  non_grabbable_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Helper function to check if a grid cell is within bounds and not an obstacle.\n  def is_walkable(x, y):\n    if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n      return False # Out of bounds\n    # Check if the cell is occupied by any non-grabbable item (which acts as an obstacle).\n    for k_idx in non_grabbable_indices:\n      if grid[x, y, k_idx] == 1:\n        return False\n    return True\n\n  # 3. Pre-compute all (x, y, direction) states from which the primitive can be collected.\n  # A state (ax, ay, adir) is \"collectable\" if:\n  #   - (ax, ay) is walkable.\n  #   - The cell (px, py) pointed to by (ax, ay, adir) contains the primitive.\n  collectable_states = set()\n\n  # Iterate through all cells in the grid to find instances of the primitive\n  for px in range(grid_width):\n    for py in range(grid_height):\n      if grid[px, py, primitive] == 1:\n        # This cell (px, py) contains the primitive.\n        # Now, find all *agent positions* (ax, ay) and *agent directions* (adir)\n        # such that the agent at (ax, ay) facing adir would point to (px, py).\n\n        # Iterate over all possible agent directions (0=UP, 1=RIGHT, 2=DOWN, 3=LEFT)\n        for adir, (dx, dy) in DIR_VEC.items():\n          # If agent is at (ax, ay) and faces (dx, dy), then (ax+dx, ay+dy) is (px, py)\n          # So, the agent's position (ax, ay) must be (px-dx, py-dy)\n          ax, ay = px - dx, py - dy\n\n          if is_walkable(ax, ay):\n            collectable_states.add((ax, ay, adir))\n\n  # If there are no collectable primitive instances on the grid or no reachable collection points,\n  # return an empty path.\n  if not collectable_states:\n      return []\n\n  # 4. Breadth-First Search (BFS)\n  # Queue stores tuples: (current_x, current_y, current_direction, list_of_actions_taken)\n  # current_direction: The direction the agent is facing *after* arriving at (current_x, current_y)\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_x, start_y, start_dir, [])])\n\n  # Visited set to avoid redundant exploration and cycles.\n  # A state is defined by (x, y, direction) because the agent's direction affects\n  # what it can interact with (via ACTION_USE).\n  visited = set([(start_x, start_y, start_dir)])\n\n  while queue:\n    curr_x, curr_y, curr_dir, path_actions = queue.popleft()\n\n    # Check if the current state is one from which the primitive can be collected.\n    if (curr_x, curr_y, curr_dir) in collectable_states:\n      return path_actions + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # Explore possible next movement actions (UP, RIGHT, DOWN, LEFT)\n    for action in [ACTION_UP, ACTION_RIGHT, ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_LEFT]:\n      # Determine the new position and direction after taking this action.\n      # The movement vector (dx, dy) corresponds to the direction integer of the action.\n      move_dx, move_dy = DIR_VEC[ACTION_TO_DIR[action]]\n      next_x, next_y = curr_x + move_dx, curr_y + move_dy\n      next_dir = ACTION_TO_DIR[action] # Agent faces the direction of its last movement\n\n      # If the next cell is walkable and this (position, direction) state hasn't been visited\n      if is_walkable(next_x, next_y) and (next_x, next_y, next_dir) not in visited:\n        visited.add((next_x, next_y, next_dir))\n        queue.append((next_x, next_y, next_dir, path_actions + [action]))\n\n  # If the queue becomes empty and no path to collect the primitive was found\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T06:57:47.310157", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    actions_taken = []\n    max_total_steps = 500  # Safety limit to prevent infinite loops\n\n    # Map relative (dx, dy) to movement actions.\n    # Assuming these movement actions also set the agent's facing direction.\n    # Dirs: 0:North(UP), 1:East(RIGHT), 2:South(DOWN), 3:West(LEFT)\n    # The (dx, dy) correspond to the relative position of a cell to move into.\n    ACTION_TO_DELTADIR = {\n        env_factory.ACTIONS.UP: (0, -1),\n        env_factory.ACTIONS.DOWN: (0, 1),\n        env_factory.ACTIONS.LEFT: (-1, 0),\n        env_factory.ACTIONS.RIGHT: (1, 0)\n    }\n\n    while len(actions_taken) < max_total_steps:\n        current_state = env._current_state\n\n        # 1. Check if the primitive is already collected\n        if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n            return actions_taken\n\n        # 2. Check if the primitive is in the 3x3 neighborhood.\n        # If `next_to` is true, we attempt to move to its cardinal position and USE.\n        if current_state.next_to(primitive):\n            # Iterate through cardinal directions to find if the primitive is a direct neighbor\n            # and if moving there would allow collection.\n            collected_nearby = False\n            for action_move, (dx, dy) in ACTION_TO_DELTADIR.items():\n                target_x = current_state.pos[0] + dx\n                target_y = current_state.pos[1] + dy\n\n                # Check bounds and if the primitive is at this cardinal neighbor cell\n                if (0 <= target_x < current_state.grid.shape[0] and\n                    0 <= target_y < current_state.grid.shape[1] and\n                    current_state.grid[target_x, target_y, primitive] > 0):\n                    \n                    # Found a primitive in a cardinal direction.\n                    # First, move towards it. This also sets the agent's facing direction.\n                    actions_taken.append(action_move)\n                    _, done, _ = env.step(action_move)\n                    if done: return actions_taken # Environment terminated unexpectedly\n\n                    # After moving, the agent is now at (target_x, target_y) and facing the direction of movement.\n                    # The primitive is now at the agent's current location, or just behind it.\n                    # Assuming USE interacts with the item at agent's new position or what it is facing.\n                    actions_taken.append(env_factory.ACTIONS.USE)\n                    _, done, _ = env.step(env_factory.ACTIONS.USE)\n                    if done: return actions_taken # Environment terminated unexpectedly\n\n                    # Re-check inventory immediately after USE attempt.\n                    if env._current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n                        return actions_taken\n                    \n                    collected_nearby = True\n                    break # Break from inner loop (found one target and tried to collect)\n            \n            if collected_nearby:\n                continue # If we attempted collection nearby, re-loop to check inventory.\n\n        # 3. If primitive not collected and not immediately next to (or previous attempt failed),\n        #    scan the entire grid to find its location.\n        primitive_x, primitive_y = -1, -1\n        grid = current_state.grid\n        WIDTH, HEIGHT, N_KINDS = grid.shape\n\n        for x in range(WIDTH):\n            for y in range(HEIGHT):\n                if grid[x, y, primitive] > 0:\n                    primitive_x, primitive_y = x, y\n                    break\n            if primitive_x != -1:\n                break\n\n        if primitive_x == -1:\n            # Primitive not found on the entire grid. Cannot collect.\n            return actions_taken\n\n        # 4. Move towards the found primitive using a simple greedy strategy (X-axis first, then Y-axis).\n        current_pos_x, current_pos_y = current_state.pos\n        \n        dx = primitive_x - current_pos_x\n        dy = primitive_y - current_pos_y\n\n        action_to_take = None\n        \n        if dx != 0:\n            action_to_take = env_factory.ACTIONS.RIGHT if dx > 0 else env_factory.ACTIONS.LEFT\n        elif dy != 0:\n            action_to_take = env_factory.ACTIONS.DOWN if dy > 0 else env_factory.ACTIONS.UP\n        \n        if action_to_take is None:\n            # Agent is at (primitive_x, primitive_y), but `next_to` block or inventory check\n            # above failed to collect it. This implies it's not grabbable by just being on it,\n            # or it requires a tool, or is a workbench. No movement action will help now.\n            return actions_taken\n\n        # Perform the chosen movement action\n        actions_taken.append(action_to_take)\n        _, done, _ = env.step(action_to_take)\n\n        if done:\n            return actions_taken # Environment terminated\n\n    return actions_taken # Max steps reached without collecting the primitive", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T06:57:48.292047", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import collections\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # Action constants (assuming these are globally defined or implicitly available)\n  DOWN = 0\n  UP = 1\n  LEFT = 2\n  RIGHT = 3\n  USE = 4\n\n  # Direction mappings (assuming these are globally defined or implicitly available)\n  # 0:N (up), 1:E (right), 2:S (down), 3:W (left)\n  DIR_DELTAS = {\n      0: (-1, 0),  # N (change in y, change in x)\n      1: (0, 1),   # E\n      2: (1, 0),   # S\n      3: (0, -1),  # W\n  }\n\n  DELTA_TO_DIR = {\n      (-1, 0): 0, # N\n      (0, 1): 1,  # E\n      (1, 0): 2,  # S\n      (0, -1): 3, # W\n  }\n\n  def _get_direction_to_face(current_pos, target_pos):\n      \"\"\"Calculates the direction an agent at current_pos needs to face to look at target_pos.\"\"\"\n      dy = target_pos[0] - current_pos[0]\n      dx = target_pos[1] - current_pos[1]\n      # Target must be immediately adjacent (Manhattan distance 1)\n      if abs(dy) + abs(dx) != 1:\n          return None # Not directly adjacent\n      return DELTA_TO_DIR.get((dy, dx))\n\n  def _get_turns(current_dir, target_dir):\n      \"\"\"Calculates minimal turning actions (LEFT/RIGHT) to change current_dir to target_dir.\"\"\"\n      actions = []\n      if current_dir == target_dir:\n          return actions\n\n      # Calculate clockwise distance (turns right)\n      dist_cw = (target_dir - current_dir + 4) % 4\n      # Calculate counter-clockwise distance (turns left)\n      dist_ccw = (current_dir - target_dir + 4) % 4\n\n      if dist_cw <= dist_ccw:\n          for _ in range(dist_cw):\n              actions.append(RIGHT)\n      else:\n          for _ in range(dist_ccw):\n              actions.append(LEFT)\n      return actions\n\n  def _is_traversable(grid, pos, non_grabbable_indices):\n      \"\"\"Checks if a given grid position is traversable by the agent (not out of bounds and not an obstacle).\"\"\"\n      y, x = pos\n      grid_height, grid_width, _ = grid.shape\n      \n      if not (0 <= y < grid_height and 0 <= x < grid_width):\n          return False # Out of bounds\n\n      # Check if the cell contains any non-grabbable entity (like wall or water)\n      # The agent cannot move into a cell occupied by a non-grabbable item.\n      for kind_idx in non_grabbable_indices:\n          if grid[y, x, kind_idx] == 1: # If this kind is present at (y,x) and is non-grabbable\n              return False\n      return True\n\n  initial_state = env._current_state\n  \n  # If the primitive is already in the inventory, no actions are needed.\n  if initial_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # BFS Queue: stores tuples of (current_simulated_state, path_taken_to_reach_this_state)\n  q = collections.deque()\n  q.append((initial_state, []))\n\n  # Visited set: stores (pos_y, pos_x, direction) to avoid cycles and redundant paths\n  visited = set()\n  visited.add((initial_state.pos[0], initial_state.pos[1], initial_state.dir))\n\n  # Maximum number of steps to search, to prevent excessively long paths or infinite loops\n  # Adjust based on expected map sizes and complexity.\n  max_steps = 200 \n\n  while q and len(q[0][1]) < max_steps:\n      current_sim_state, current_path = q.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the primitive can be collected from the current simulated state\n      # The USE action applies to the cell directly in front of the agent.\n      # So, we need to find if a primitive is in an adjacent cell.\n      for dy, dx in [(0, 1), (0, -1), (1, 0), (-1, 0)]: # Deltas for N, S, E, W relative to agent's position\n          neighbor_pos = (current_sim_state.pos[0] + dy, current_sim_state.pos[1] + dx)\n          ny, nx = neighbor_pos\n\n          grid_height, grid_width, _ = current_sim_state.grid.shape\n          if not (0 <= ny < grid_height and 0 <= nx < grid_width):\n              continue # Out of bounds\n\n          # Check if the primitive is at the neighbor position\n          if current_sim_state.grid[ny, nx, primitive] == 1:\n              # Primitive found at neighbor_pos. Calculate actions to face it and USE.\n              target_dir = _get_direction_to_face(current_sim_state.pos, neighbor_pos)\n              \n              if target_dir is not None: # Should always be not None for direct (dy,dx) deltas\n                  turning_actions = _get_turns(current_sim_state.dir, target_dir)\n                  \n                  # Simulate applying the turning actions\n                  temp_state_after_turns = current_sim_state\n                  for action in turning_actions:\n                      # CraftState.step returns (reward, new_state)\n                      _, temp_state_after_turns = temp_state_after_turns.step(action)\n                  \n                  # Simulate applying the USE action\n                  _, state_after_use = temp_state_after_turns.step(USE)\n                  \n                  # Check if the primitive was successfully collected after USE\n                  if state_after_use.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n                      return current_path + turning_actions + [USE]\n\n      # Explore valid move actions (DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT)\n      for action in [DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT]:\n          # Simulate the action to get the next state\n          _, next_sim_state = current_sim_state.step(action)\n          next_pos = next_sim_state.pos\n          next_dir = next_sim_state.dir\n\n          # Check if the next position is traversable (not a wall/water etc.)\n          if _is_traversable(next_sim_state.grid, next_pos, env.world.non_grabbable_indices):\n              state_key = (next_pos[0], next_pos[1], next_dir)\n              if state_key not in visited:\n                  visited.add(state_key)\n                  q.append((next_sim_state, current_path + [action]))\n\n  # If no path is found within the max_steps limit, return an empty list\n  return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T06:59:27.797115", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    initial_state = env._current_state\n    start_pos_x, start_pos_y = initial_state.pos\n    start_dir = initial_state.dir\n    grid = initial_state.grid\n    width, height, _ = grid.shape # Extract grid dimensions\n\n    # Determine if the primitive is grabbable or non-grabbable.\n    # Non-grabbable items are typically structures like workbenches, water, or lava.\n    # Grabbable items can be picked up from the same square.\n    non_grabbable_indices = initial_state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n    is_primitive_grabbable = primitive not in non_grabbable_indices\n\n    # Action constants\n    ACTION_DOWN = 0\n    ACTION_UP = 1\n    ACTION_LEFT = 2\n    ACTION_RIGHT = 3\n    ACTION_USE = 4\n    ACTIONS_MOVEMENT = [ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_UP, ACTION_LEFT, ACTION_RIGHT]\n\n    # Direction constants (matching CraftWorld's internal representation)\n    DIR_NORTH = 0\n    DIR_EAST = 1\n    DIR_SOUTH = 2\n    DIR_WEST = 3\n\n    # Mapping movement actions to (delta_x, delta_y) for position change and resulting new direction\n    ACTION_TO_DELTAS_AND_DIR = {\n        ACTION_UP: (0, -1, DIR_NORTH),\n        ACTION_DOWN: (0, 1, DIR_SOUTH),\n        ACTION_LEFT: (-1, 0, DIR_WEST),\n        ACTION_RIGHT: (1, 0, DIR_EAST),\n    }\n\n    # Mapping agent's current direction to (delta_x, delta_y) for the cell directly in front\n    DIR_TO_DELTAS = {\n        DIR_NORTH: (0, -1),\n        DIR_EAST: (1, 0),\n        DIR_SOUTH: (0, 1),\n        DIR_WEST: (-1, 0),\n    }\n\n    # Helper function to check if a cell is blocked for agent movement\n    def is_blocked(x, y):\n        if not (0 <= x < width and 0 <= y < height):\n            return True  # Out of bounds\n        # A cell is blocked if it contains any non-grabbable item\n        for i_kind in non_grabbable_indices:\n            if grid[x, y, i_kind] > 0:\n                return True\n        return False\n\n    min_actions_len = float('inf')\n    best_actions = []\n\n    # BFS setup\n    queue = collections.deque()\n    # Visited set stores (x, y, dir) tuples to avoid redundant exploration and cycles\n    visited = set()\n\n    # Initial state: (current_position_x, current_position_y, current_direction), [actions_taken_so_far]\n    queue.append(((start_pos_x, start_pos_y, start_dir), []))\n    visited.add((start_pos_x, start_pos_y, start_dir))\n\n    while queue:\n        (curr_x, curr_y, curr_dir), actions_so_far = queue.popleft()\n        current_path_len = len(actions_so_far)\n\n        # Optimization: If the current path (including a potential USE action)\n        # is already longer than or equal to the shortest found path, prune this branch.\n        if current_path_len + 1 >= min_actions_len:\n            continue\n\n        # Check if the goal (collecting the primitive) can be satisfied from this state\n        goal_satisfied = False\n        candidate_actions = []\n\n        if is_primitive_grabbable:\n            # If the primitive is grabbable, the agent needs to be on the same square as the primitive\n            if grid[curr_x, curr_y, primitive] > 0:\n                goal_satisfied = True\n                candidate_actions = actions_so_far + [ACTION_USE]\n        else:\n            # If the primitive is non-grabbable, the agent needs to be adjacent to it and facing it\n            dx_front, dy_front = DIR_TO_DELTAS[curr_dir]\n            front_x, front_y = curr_x + dx_front, curr_y + dy_front\n\n            # Check if the cell directly in front of the agent contains the target primitive\n            if (0 <= front_x < width and 0 <= front_y < height and\n                grid[front_x, front_y, primitive] > 0):\n                goal_satisfied = True\n                candidate_actions = actions_so_far + [ACTION_USE]\n        \n        # If a path to collect the primitive is found from the current state\n        if goal_satisfied:\n            if len(candidate_actions) < min_actions_len:\n                min_actions_len = len(candidate_actions)\n                best_actions = candidate_actions\n            # Continue BFS exploration. Even if a goal is found, there might be\n            # another instance of the primitive or another path to it that is shorter overall.\n            # The `min_actions_len` pruning above will ensure we only explore promising paths.\n\n        # Explore movement actions from the current state\n        for action in ACTIONS_MOVEMENT:\n            delta_x, delta_y, new_dir = ACTION_TO_DELTAS_AND_DIR[action]\n            next_x, next_y = curr_x + delta_x, curr_y + delta_y\n\n            # Only add to queue if this path (movement + potential future USE) could be shorter\n            if current_path_len + 1 < min_actions_len:\n                if not is_blocked(next_x, next_y):\n                    next_state_tuple = (next_x, next_y, new_dir)\n                    if next_state_tuple not in visited:\n                        visited.add(next_state_tuple)\n                        queue.append((next_state_tuple, actions_so_far + [action]))\n\n    return best_actions", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T06:59:27.875846", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    import collections\n\n    # Get essential information from the environment\n    current_state = env._current_state\n    world = env.world\n    action_map = env.action_specs()\n\n    # Define action IDs for clarity\n    ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n    ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n    ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n    ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n    ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n    # Grid dimensions\n    WIDTH, HEIGHT = current_state.grid.shape[:2]\n\n    # Check if the primitive is already in inventory\n    if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n        return [] # Primitive already collected\n\n    # Determine if the primitive is grabbable. If not, it cannot be \"collected\" into inventory.\n    # The `grabbable_indices` in CraftWorld indicates items that can be picked up.\n    if primitive not in world.grabbable_indices:\n        return [] # Cannot collect this item type\n\n    # Pre-calculate target cells: any cell (tx, ty) from which the agent can `USE`\n    # and successfully pick up the primitive. This means (tx, ty) must be\n    # cardinally adjacent to a cell containing the primitive.\n    target_cells = set()\n    \n    # Find all locations on the grid where the primitive exists\n    # np.argwhere returns (row, col) which translates to (y, x) if grid is (H, W)\n    # but based on common numpy usage for (W, H), it's (x, y) if the first index is width.\n    # Given the shape (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds), grid[x, y] is the correct access.\n    primitive_locations = np.argwhere(current_state.grid[:, :, primitive] > 0)\n\n    # For each found primitive location, identify its valid adjacent cells\n    for px, py in primitive_locations:\n        # Check 4 cardinal neighbors: (x-1,y), (x+1,y), (x,y-1), (x,y+1)\n        for dx, dy in [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]:\n            tx, ty = px + dx, py + dy\n            # Ensure the target adjacent cell is within grid bounds\n            if 0 <= tx < WIDTH and 0 <= ty < HEIGHT:\n                target_cells.add((tx, ty))\n    \n    # If no primitive items are found on the grid, or no valid adjacent cells, it's uncollectable\n    if not target_cells:\n        return []\n\n    # BFS for shortest path to any target_cell\n    # Queue stores tuples: (current_position, list_of_actions_taken_to_reach_here)\n    q = collections.deque([(current_state.pos, [])]) \n    \n    # Keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles and ensure shortest path\n    visited = {current_state.pos} \n\n    while q:\n        curr_pos, path = q.popleft()\n        curr_x, curr_y = curr_pos\n\n        # Check if the current position is one of our target cells\n        if curr_pos in target_cells:\n            # We have reached a position from which we can collect the primitive.\n            # The `next_to` method in CraftState does not depend on the agent's direction,\n            # implying that `USE` interacts with any adjacent item.\n            path.append(ACTION_USE)\n            return path\n\n        # Define possible moves and their corresponding new positions\n        # These are absolute grid movements, not relative to agent's facing direction.\n        possible_moves = [\n            (ACTION_UP, (curr_x, curr_y - 1)),\n            (ACTION_DOWN, (curr_x, curr_y + 1)),\n            (ACTION_LEFT, (curr_x - 1, curr_y)),\n            (ACTION_RIGHT, (curr_x + 1, curr_y))\n        ]\n\n        for action, next_pos in possible_moves:\n            next_x, next_y = next_pos\n            # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries\n            if 0 <= next_x < WIDTH and 0 <= next_y < HEIGHT:\n                # Check if this position has been visited already to avoid redundant paths\n                if next_pos not in visited:\n                    visited.add(next_pos)\n                    q.append((next_pos, path + [action]))\n\n    # If the queue is exhausted and no path to a target cell was found\n    return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:01:04.865268", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    import collections\n\n    # Get the current state directly from the environment's internal state\n    # This assumes direct access to `_current_state` is permitted for efficiency\n    # within this internal function, as opposed to parsing `observations()`.\n    state = env._current_state\n\n    # 1. Check if the primitive is already in the inventory\n    if state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n        return []\n\n    # 2. Check if the agent is already adjacent to (or on) the primitive\n    # In this case, only the USE action is needed.\n    if state.next_to(primitive):\n        return [env_factory.ACTIONS.USE]\n\n    # If not already collected or adjacent, we need to pathfind.\n\n    # Access CraftWorld instance for environment details, specifically non-grabbable items\n    world = env.world\n    # `non_grabbable_indices` identifies entities that act as obstacles (cannot be walked onto)\n    obstacle_indices = world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n    # Get grid dimensions (rows, columns)\n    GRID_HEIGHT, GRID_WIDTH, _ = state.grid.shape\n\n    # Helper function to determine if a cell is traversable\n    def is_traversable(r, c, grid_data, obstacles_set):\n        # Check if coordinates are within grid boundaries\n        if not (0 <= r < GRID_HEIGHT and 0 <= c < GRID_WIDTH):\n            return False\n\n        # Check if the cell contains any obstacle\n        for obstacle_idx in obstacles_set:\n            if grid_data[r, c, obstacle_idx] == 1:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    # Define possible cardinal moves and their corresponding (row_change, col_change)\n    MOVES = {\n        env_factory.ACTIONS.UP: (-1, 0),\n        env_factory.ACTIONS.DOWN: (1, 0),\n        env_factory.ACTIONS.LEFT: (0, -1),\n        env_factory.ACTIONS.RIGHT: (0, 1),\n    }\n\n    # Find all locations on the grid where the primitive exists\n    primitive_locations = np.argwhere(state.grid[:, :, primitive] == 1)\n\n    if len(primitive_locations) == 0:\n        # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the grid, it cannot be collected\n        return []\n\n    # Determine all possible \"goal cells\" - these are traversable cells from which\n    # the agent can perform a 'USE' action to collect the primitive.\n    # This means any traversable cell in the 3x3 neighborhood of a primitive location,\n    # excluding the primitive's own cell if it's not traversable.\n    goal_cells = set()\n    for pr, pc in primitive_locations:\n        # Iterate through the 3x3 neighborhood (including diagonals)\n        for dr_offset in [-1, 0, 1]:\n            for dc_offset in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                # Skip the primitive's own cell (pr, pc) as we are looking for a cell\n                # to *move to* before using 'USE'. If agent is on it, `state.next_to` handles.\n                if dr_offset == 0 and dc_offset == 0:\n                    continue \n\n                nr, nc = pr + dr_offset, pc + dc_offset\n                # If the neighboring cell is traversable, it's a valid goal cell\n                if is_traversable(nr, nc, state.grid, obstacle_indices):\n                    goal_cells.add((nr, nc))\n\n    if not goal_cells:\n        # If no traversable adjacent cells can be found for any primitive,\n        # it's impossible to reach a \"use\" position.\n        return []\n\n    # Perform a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path to any goal cell\n    # The queue stores tuples: (current_position_tuple, list_of_actions_to_reach_current_position)\n    queue = collections.deque([(state.pos, [])]) \n    # The visited set keeps track of positions already explored to prevent cycles and redundant paths\n    visited = {state.pos}\n\n    while queue:\n        (r, c), path = queue.popleft()\n\n        # If the current position is one of our goal cells\n        if (r, c) in goal_cells:\n            # We've found the shortest path to a cell from which we can collect.\n            # Append the 'USE' action to the path and return the sequence.\n            return path + [env_factory.ACTIONS.USE]\n\n        # Explore all four cardinal neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT)\n        for action, (dr, dc) in MOVES.items():\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n            next_pos = (nr, nc)\n\n            # Check if the next position is traversable and has not been visited yet\n            if is_traversable(nr, nc, state.grid, obstacle_indices) and next_pos not in visited:\n                visited.add(next_pos)\n                queue.append((next_pos, path + [action]))\n\n    # If the BFS completes and no path was found to any goal cell,\n    # it means the primitive is unreachable from the current state.\n    return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:01:04.934489", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    initial_state = env._current_state\n    \n    # 1. Initial Check: If primitive already in inventory, return empty list.\n    if initial_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n        return []\n\n    # BFS Queue: stores (current_CraftState_instance, list_of_actions_taken)\n    queue = collections.deque([(initial_state, [])])\n\n    # Visited set: stores hashable representation of a state to avoid cycles and redundant computation.\n    # A state is defined by (position_tuple, direction_int, inventory_tuple).\n    # Inventory is important because the effect of 'USE' changes it, leading to a new \"state\".\n    # Grid state is assumed to be static for the purpose of finding the primitive,\n    # and only changes after a successful 'USE' action on the item.\n    visited = set()\n    \n    # Maximum number of steps to search, to prevent excessively long or infinite searches.\n    # This is a heuristic to bound computation time for potentially large state spaces.\n    MAX_SEARCH_DEPTH = 200 # Adjust based on expected grid size and complexity\n\n    while queue:\n        current_state, actions_taken = queue.popleft()\n\n        # Create a unique key for the current state to check against 'visited' set.\n        # Convert numpy array inventory to tuple for hashing.\n        current_state_key = (current_state.pos, current_state.dir, tuple(current_state.inventory))\n\n        if current_state_key in visited:\n            continue # Already visited this exact state via a shorter or equal path\n        visited.add(current_state_key)\n\n        # Check for search depth limit\n        if len(actions_taken) >= MAX_SEARCH_DEPTH:\n            continue # Prune this path, it's too long\n\n        # Explore possible next states by taking all available actions\n        # Actions include movement (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT) and USE.\n        # Assuming constants ACTION_UP, ACTION_DOWN, etc. are defined elsewhere or known.\n        # Based on action_specs: DOWN=0, UP=1, LEFT=2, RIGHT=3, USE=4\n        possible_actions = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4] # Corresponds to DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT, USE\n        \n        for action in possible_actions:\n            # Simulate taking the action to get the next state.\n            # CraftState.step returns a *new* CraftState instance, which is crucial for BFS.\n            # The reward returned by step is not needed for pathfinding here.\n            _, next_state = current_state.step(action) \n\n            # If the action resulted in no change in position, direction, and inventory\n            # (e.g., hit a wall, attempted USE on nothing or an uncollectible item),\n            # this path segment is effectively a no-op. We can skip such paths to optimize.\n            if (next_state.pos == current_state.pos and\n                next_state.dir == current_state.dir and\n                np.array_equal(next_state.inventory, current_state.inventory)):\n                continue \n\n            # Check if the primitive has been collected in the next_state.\n            if next_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n                # Goal achieved! Return the sequence of actions that led to this state.\n                return actions_taken + [action]\n            \n            # If the primitive is not yet collected, add the next_state to the queue\n            # for further exploration. The 'visited' check will prevent redundant processing\n            # when this state is later popped from the queue.\n            queue.append((next_state, actions_taken + [action]))\n\n    # If the queue becomes empty and no path was found (primitive not collectible within depth limit)\n    return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:02:08.338664", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import collections\n\n  # Constants as defined in collect_v1, ensuring consistency\n  ACTION_DOWN = 0\n  ACTION_UP = 1\n  ACTION_LEFT = 2\n  ACTION_RIGHT = 3\n  ACTION_USE = 4\n\n  # Map action to its corresponding direction integer (0:UP, 1:RIGHT, 2:DOWN, 3:LEFT)\n  # This mapping specifies the direction the agent faces *after* taking the movement action.\n  ACTION_TO_DIR = {\n      ACTION_UP: 0,    # Action 1 (UP) leads to facing direction 0 (UP)\n      ACTION_RIGHT: 1, # Action 3 (RIGHT) leads to facing direction 1 (RIGHT)\n      ACTION_DOWN: 2,  # Action 0 (DOWN) leads to facing direction 2 (DOWN)\n      ACTION_LEFT: 3   # Action 2 (LEFT) leads to facing direction 3 (LEFT)\n  }\n\n  # Map direction integer to its (dx, dy) vector (change in position)\n  DIR_VEC = {\n      0: (0, -1),  # UP: decreases y coordinate\n      1: (1, 0),   # RIGHT: increases x coordinate\n      2: (0, 1),   # DOWN: increases y coordinate\n      3: (-1, 0)   # LEFT: decreases x coordinate\n  }\n\n  # 1. Pre-checks: If the primitive is not a grabbable item, it cannot be \"collected\".\n  if primitive not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # Get initial state information\n  initial_state = env._current_state\n  start_x, start_y = initial_state.pos\n  start_dir = initial_state.dir # Agent's initial facing direction\n  grid = initial_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  non_grabbable_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Helper function to check if a grid cell is within bounds and not an obstacle.\n  def is_walkable(x, y):\n    if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n      return False # Out of bounds\n    # Check if the cell is occupied by any non-grabbable item (obstacle).\n    for k_idx in non_grabbable_indices:\n      if grid[x, y, k_idx] == 1:\n        return False\n    return True\n\n  # 2. Pre-compute all potential agent collection states (x, y, direction).\n  # Unlike collect_v1, this version assumes ACTION_USE requires the agent to be\n  # facing the item. Therefore, a target state is (agent_x, agent_y, agent_direction)\n  # such that the cell directly in front of (agent_x, agent_y) when facing agent_direction\n  # contains the 'primitive'.\n  target_agent_states = set()\n  \n  # Iterate through every cell in the grid\n  for px in range(grid_width):\n    for py in range(grid_height):\n      # If this cell (px, py) contains the primitive\n      if grid[px, py, primitive] == 1:\n        # For each possible direction the agent could be facing\n        for ad in [0, 1, 2, 3]: # 0:UP, 1:RIGHT, 2:DOWN, 3:LEFT\n          # Calculate the required agent position (ax, ay)\n          # If (px, py) is (ax + dx, ay + dy), then (ax, ay) = (px - dx, py - dy)\n          dx, dy = DIR_VEC[ad]\n          ax, ay = px - dx, py - dy\n\n          # Check if this potential agent position is walkable and within bounds.\n          if is_walkable(ax, ay):\n            target_agent_states.add((ax, ay, ad))\n  \n  # If no primitive is found, or no walkable spots/directions around primitives, return empty path\n  if not target_agent_states:\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Breadth-First Search (BFS) for the shortest path to any target_agent_state.\n  # Queue stores tuples: (current_x, current_y, current_direction, list_of_actions_taken)\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_x, start_y, start_dir, [])])\n\n  # Visited set to avoid redundant exploration and cycles.\n  # A state in the BFS is defined by (x, y, direction).\n  visited = set([(start_x, start_y, start_dir)])\n\n  while queue:\n    curr_x, curr_y, curr_dir, path_actions = queue.popleft()\n\n    # Check if the current agent state (position and direction) matches one of the pre-computed target states.\n    if (curr_x, curr_y, curr_dir) in target_agent_states:\n      # If so, we've found the shortest path to a suitable collection spot and facing direction.\n      # Append the ACTION_USE to complete the collection.\n      return path_actions + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # Explore possible next movement actions (UP, RIGHT, DOWN, LEFT)\n    for action in [ACTION_UP, ACTION_RIGHT, ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_LEFT]:\n      # Determine the new direction the agent will face after taking this movement action.\n      next_dir = ACTION_TO_DIR[action]\n      \n      # Determine the new position based on the new facing direction.\n      move_dx, move_dy = DIR_VEC[next_dir]\n      next_x, next_y = curr_x + move_dx, curr_y + move_dy\n\n      # If the next cell is walkable and this specific (position, direction) state hasn't been visited yet\n      if is_walkable(next_x, next_y) and (next_x, next_y, next_dir) not in visited:\n        visited.add((next_x, next_y, next_dir))\n        queue.append((next_x, next_y, next_dir, path_actions + [action]))\n\n  # If the queue becomes empty and no path to collect the primitive was found\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:02:09.330928", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import collections\n\n  ACTION_DOWN = 0\n  ACTION_UP = 1\n  ACTION_LEFT = 2\n  ACTION_RIGHT = 3\n  ACTION_USE = 4\n\n  # Map action to its corresponding direction integer (0:UP, 1:RIGHT, 2:DOWN, 3:LEFT)\n  ACTION_TO_DIR = {\n      ACTION_UP: 0,\n      ACTION_RIGHT: 1,\n      ACTION_DOWN: 2,\n      ACTION_LEFT: 3\n  }\n\n  # Map direction integer to its (dx, dy) vector (change in position)\n  # These vectors represent the change in agent's coordinates when moving in a given direction.\n  DIR_VEC = {\n      0: (0, -1),  # UP: decreases y\n      1: (1, 0),   # RIGHT: increases x\n      2: (0, 1),   # DOWN: increases y\n      3: (-1, 0)   # LEFT: decreases x\n  }\n\n  # 1. Pre-checks: If the primitive is not a grabbable item, it cannot be \"collected\".\n  if primitive not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # Get initial state information\n  initial_state = env._current_state\n  start_x, start_y = initial_state.pos\n  start_dir = initial_state.dir # Initial facing direction\n  grid = initial_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n  non_grabbable_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # Helper function to check if a grid cell is within bounds and not an obstacle.\n  def is_walkable(x, y):\n    if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n      return False # Out of bounds\n    # Check if the cell is occupied by any non-grabbable item (obstacle).\n    for k_idx in non_grabbable_indices:\n      if grid[x, y, k_idx] == 1:\n        return False\n    return True\n\n  # 2. Pre-compute all potential agent \"target states\" for collection.\n  # An \"improved\" assumption for collect_v2 is that ACTION_USE requires the agent\n  # to be facing the item it intends to collect.\n  # A target state is (agent_x, agent_y, agent_direction) from which ACTION_USE\n  # can directly collect the primitive because the primitive is in front of the agent.\n  target_agent_states = set()\n  \n  # Iterate through every cell in the grid to find primitive locations.\n  for px in range(grid_width):\n    for py in range(grid_height):\n      # If this cell (px, py) contains the primitive\n      if grid[px, py, primitive] == 1:\n        # For each possible facing direction of the agent (0:UP, 1:RIGHT, 2:DOWN, 3:LEFT)\n        for agent_facing_dir in [0, 1, 2, 3]:\n          # Calculate the agent's required position (ax, ay) such that\n          # if the agent at (ax, ay) faces 'agent_facing_dir', then (px, py) is directly in front.\n          # The cell in front is (ax + dx_front, ay + dy_front), where (dx_front, dy_front) is DIR_VEC[agent_facing_dir].\n          # So, (ax, ay) must be (px - dx_front, py - dy_front).\n          dx_front, dy_front = DIR_VEC[agent_facing_dir]\n          ax, ay = px - dx_front, py - dy_front\n\n          # Check if this potential agent position is walkable.\n          if is_walkable(ax, ay):\n            target_agent_states.add((ax, ay, agent_facing_dir))\n  \n  # If no primitive is found on the grid, or no walkable spots from which to collect it, return empty path.\n  if not target_agent_states:\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Breadth-First Search (BFS) for shortest path to any target_agent_state.\n  # Queue stores tuples: (current_x, current_y, current_direction, list_of_actions_taken)\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_x, start_y, start_dir, [])])\n\n  # Visited set to avoid redundant exploration and cycles.\n  # A state is defined by (x, y, direction).\n  visited = set([(start_x, start_y, start_dir)])\n\n  while queue:\n    curr_x, curr_y, curr_dir, path_actions = queue.popleft()\n\n    # Check if the current agent state (position AND direction) is one of the pre-computed target states.\n    if (curr_x, curr_y, curr_dir) in target_agent_states:\n      # If so, we've found the shortest path to a suitable collection spot with the correct orientation.\n      # Append the ACTION_USE to complete the collection.\n      return path_actions + [ACTION_USE]\n\n    # Explore possible next movement actions (UP, RIGHT, DOWN, LEFT)\n    for action in [ACTION_UP, ACTION_RIGHT, ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_LEFT]:\n      # Determine the new position and direction after taking this action\n      move_dx, move_dy = DIR_VEC[ACTION_TO_DIR[action]]\n      next_x, next_y = curr_x + move_dx, curr_y + move_dy\n      next_dir = ACTION_TO_DIR[action] # Agent's new facing direction is determined by the movement action.\n\n      # If the next cell is walkable and this (position, direction) state hasn't been visited\n      if is_walkable(next_x, next_y) and (next_x, next_y, next_dir) not in visited:\n        visited.add((next_x, next_y, next_dir))\n        queue.append((next_x, next_y, next_dir, path_actions + [action]))\n\n  # If the queue becomes empty and no path to collect the primitive was found\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:03:55.750717", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import collections\n\n  # Define action constants within the function scope.\n  DOWN = 0\n  UP = 1\n  LEFT = 2\n  RIGHT = 3\n  USE = 4\n\n  state = env._current_state\n  \n  # If the primitive is already in the inventory, no actions are needed.\n  if state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  grid = state.grid\n  WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n  start_pos = state.pos\n\n  # Get indices of entities that cannot be walked through (obstacles).\n  non_grabbable_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n  # BFS to find the shortest path to a cell *adjacent* to any instance of the primitive.\n  # The queue stores tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_current_position).\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])])\n  # Keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles and redundant processing.\n  visited = {start_pos}\n\n  # Define possible cardinal movements and their corresponding actions.\n  # (dx, dy) -> action_id\n  cardinal_moves = {\n      (0, 1): DOWN,\n      (0, -1): UP,\n      (1, 0): RIGHT,\n      (-1, 0): LEFT\n  }\n\n  # Perform BFS\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path_actions = queue.popleft()\n      \n      # Check if the current_pos is adjacent to any instance of the primitive.\n      # An agent can USE an item if it's in its 3x3 neighborhood (including diagonals).\n      for dx_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          for dy_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              if dx_adj == 0 and dy_adj == 0:\n                  continue # Skip the current position itself\n\n              neighbor_x, neighbor_y = current_pos[0] + dx_adj, current_pos[1] + dy_adj\n\n              # Check if the potential primitive location (neighbor) is within grid boundaries.\n              if not (0 <= neighbor_x < WIDTH and 0 <= neighbor_y < HEIGHT):\n                  continue\n\n              # If this neighbor cell contains the primitive, then current_pos is adjacent.\n              if grid[neighbor_x, neighbor_y, primitive] > 0:\n                  # Found a path to a position from which the primitive can be collected.\n                  # Append the USE action and return the complete sequence of actions.\n                  return path_actions + [USE]\n\n      # If not adjacent to the primitive, explore valid neighboring cells for movement.\n      for move_diff, action in cardinal_moves.items():\n          dx, dy = move_diff\n          next_x, next_y = current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy\n          next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n          # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries.\n          if not (0 <= next_x < WIDTH and 0 <= next_y < HEIGHT):\n              continue\n          \n          # Check if the next position is an obstacle (contains a non-grabbable item).\n          is_obstacle = False\n          for obstacle_idx in non_grabbable_indices:\n              if grid[next_x, next_y, obstacle_idx] > 0:\n                  is_obstacle = True\n                  break\n          if is_obstacle:\n              continue\n\n          # If the next position is valid and has not been visited, add it to the queue.\n          if next_pos not in visited:\n              visited.add(next_pos)\n              queue.append((next_pos, path_actions + [action]))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and no path to an adjacent primitive is found, return an empty list.\n  return []", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:03:56.830958", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  MAX_TOTAL_STEPS = 250  # A generous limit to prevent infinite loops\n\n  actions_taken = []\n  obs = env.reset()\n  current_pos = tuple(obs['features_dict']['pos'])\n  inventory = obs['features_dict']['inventory']\n\n  # Check if primitive is already in inventory\n  if inventory[primitive] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Store visited positions to detect getting stuck in simple loops\n  visited_positions = set()\n  visited_positions.add(current_pos)\n\n  for step_count in range(MAX_TOTAL_STEPS):\n    # 1. Check if goal is satisfied (primitive collected)\n    if obs['features_dict']['inventory'][primitive] > 0:\n      return actions_taken\n\n    # 2. Check if primitive is next to agent and can be used\n    if env._current_state.next_to(primitive):\n      reward, done, obs = env.step(env_factory.ACTIONS.USE)\n      actions_taken.append(env_factory.ACTIONS.USE)\n      # After USE, re-check inventory immediately, as it might be collected\n      if obs['features_dict']['inventory'][primitive] > 0:\n        return actions_taken\n      continue  # Try to collect, then re-evaluate position/goal\n\n    # 3. If not next to it, find the closest primitive location\n    current_pos = tuple(obs['features_dict']['pos'])\n    grid = obs['features_dict']['features_global']\n    primitive_locations = np.argwhere(grid[:, :, primitive] > 0)\n\n    if len(primitive_locations) == 0:\n      # Primitive not found on the map or vanished (e.g., already collected, despawned)\n      # If not in inventory (checked at start), means it's uncollectable/unavailable.\n      return actions_taken\n\n    closest_loc = None\n    min_dist = float('inf')\n    for loc_array in primitive_locations:\n      # np.argwhere returns [x_coord, y_coord] if grid is (WIDTH, HEIGHT, KINDS)\n      t_x, t_y = loc_array[0], loc_array[1]\n      p_x, p_y = current_pos\n      dist = abs(t_x - p_x) + abs(t_y - p_y) # Manhattan distance\n      if dist < min_dist:\n        min_dist = dist\n        closest_loc = (t_x, t_y) # Store as tuple for consistency\n\n    target_pos = closest_loc # (tx, ty)\n\n    # 4. Determine best movement action\n    p_x, p_y = current_pos\n    t_x, t_y = target_pos\n\n    dx = t_x - p_x\n    dy = t_y - p_y\n\n    chosen_action = None\n\n    # Prioritize movement along the axis with the larger distance to cover.\n    if abs(dx) >= abs(dy): # Prefer horizontal movement if dx is larger or equal\n      if dx > 0:\n        chosen_action = env_factory.ACTIONS.RIGHT\n      elif dx < 0:\n        chosen_action = env_factory.ACTIONS.LEFT\n      else: # dx is 0, so only dy matters\n        if dy > 0:\n          chosen_action = env_factory.ACTIONS.DOWN\n        elif dy < 0:\n          chosen_action = env_factory.ACTIONS.UP\n    else: # abs(dy) > abs(dx), prefer vertical movement\n      if dy > 0:\n        chosen_action = env_factory.ACTIONS.DOWN\n      elif dy < 0:\n        chosen_action = env_factory.ACTIONS.UP\n      else: # dy is 0, so only dx matters (should be covered by first if)\n          if dx > 0:\n              chosen_action = env_factory.ACTIONS.RIGHT\n          elif dx < 0:\n              chosen_action = env_factory.ACTIONS.LEFT\n\n    # If chosen_action is None, it means dx=0 and dy=0, agent is at target but not collected.\n    if chosen_action is None:\n        return actions_taken # Cannot move, or target is unreachable/uncollectable.\n\n    # Attempt the chosen action\n    prev_pos = current_pos\n    reward, done, new_obs = env.step(chosen_action)\n    actions_taken.append(chosen_action)\n    current_pos = tuple(new_obs['features_dict']['pos'])\n    obs = new_obs\n\n    # If movement was blocked (position did not change), try an alternative action\n    if current_pos == prev_pos:\n      alt_action = None\n      \n      # If primary move failed, try a perpendicular move.\n      # Prioritize the other axis if there's still a distance to cover there.\n      if (chosen_action == env_factory.ACTIONS.RIGHT or chosen_action == env_factory.ACTIONS.LEFT): # Tried horizontal\n        if dy > 0:\n          alt_action = env_factory.ACTIONS.DOWN\n        elif dy < 0:\n          alt_action = env_factory.ACTIONS.UP\n      else: # Must have tried UP or DOWN (vertical)\n        if dx > 0:\n          alt_action = env_factory.ACTIONS.RIGHT\n        elif dx < 0:\n          alt_action = env_factory.ACTIONS.LEFT\n      \n      # If no perpendicular direction with target, try moving in the *opposite* direction on the same axis\n      # This is a very basic attempt to go around an obstacle if perpendicular isn't an option or also blocked.\n      if alt_action is None:\n          if chosen_action == env_factory.ACTIONS.RIGHT: alt_action = env_factory.ACTIONS.LEFT\n          elif chosen_action == env_factory.ACTIONS.LEFT: alt_action = env_factory.ACTIONS.RIGHT\n          elif chosen_action == env_factory.ACTIONS.UP: alt_action = env_factory.ACTIONS.DOWN\n          elif chosen_action == env_factory.ACTIONS.DOWN: alt_action = env_factory.ACTIONS.UP\n\n      if alt_action is not None:\n        prev_pos = current_pos # Still at the stuck position\n        reward, done, new_obs = env.step(alt_action)\n        actions_taken.append(alt_action)\n        current_pos = tuple(new_obs['features_dict']['pos'])\n        obs = new_obs\n\n        if current_pos == prev_pos:\n          # Still stuck after alternative move. Simple avoidance failed.\n          return actions_taken # Give up, as it's likely a complex blockage.\n      else:\n        # No alternative action found (e.g., target on same axis, no perpendicular direction).\n        return actions_taken # Give up\n\n    # If the agent moved to a new position, add it to visited.\n    # If it moved to an already visited position, it might be looping.\n    # The MAX_TOTAL_STEPS limit will eventually catch infinite loops.\n    if current_pos not in visited_positions:\n        visited_positions.add(current_pos)\n\n  # If MAX_TOTAL_STEPS reached and primitive not collected\n  return actions_taken", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:04:34.165202", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:04:35.183741", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import collections\n\n  ACTION_DOWN = 0\n  ACTION_UP = 1\n  ACTION_LEFT = 2\n  ACTION_RIGHT = 3\n  ACTION_USE = 4\n\n  # Map action to its corresponding direction integer (0:UP, 1:RIGHT, 2:DOWN, 3:LEFT)\n  ACTION_TO_DIR = {\n      ACTION_UP: 0,\n      ACTION_RIGHT: 1,\n      ACTION_DOWN: 2,\n      ACTION_LEFT: 3\n  }\n\n  # Map direction integer to its (dx, dy) vector (change in position)\n  DIR_VEC = {\n      0: (0, -1),  # UP: decreases y\n      1: (1, 0),   # RIGHT: increases x\n      2: (0, 1),   # DOWN: increases y\n      3: (-1, 0)   # LEFT: decreases x\n  }\n\n  # 1. Pre-checks: If the primitive is not a grabbable item, it cannot be \"collected\".\n  if primitive not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n    return []\n\n  # Get current state information\n  initial_state = env._current_state\n  start_x, start_y = initial_state.pos\n  start_dir = initial_state.dir # Agent's initial facing direction (0, 1, 2, or 3)\n  grid = initial_state.grid\n  grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Helper function to check if a grid cell is within bounds and not an obstacle.\n  def is_walkable(x, y):\n    if not (0 <= x < grid_width and 0 <= y < grid_height):\n      return False # Out of bounds\n    # Check if the cell is occupied by a non-grabbable item (which acts as an obstacle).\n    for k_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n      if grid[x, y, k_idx] == 1:\n        return False\n    return True\n\n  # 2. Breadth-First Search (BFS) for shortest path\n  # Queue stores tuples: (current_x, current_y, current_direction)\n  # This stores the state (position and facing direction) of the agent.\n  queue = collections.deque([(start_x, start_y, start_dir)])\n\n  # Visited set to avoid redundant exploration and cycles.\n  # A state is defined by (x, y, direction).\n  visited = set([(start_x, start_y, start_dir)])\n\n  # Parent map for path reconstruction:\n  # Stores {current_state: (parent_state, action_to_reach_current_state)}\n  parent_map = {}\n\n  # Variable to store the state from which the 'USE' action can be taken\n  goal_reached_state = None\n\n  while queue:\n    curr_x, curr_y, curr_dir = queue.popleft()\n\n    # Check if the primitive is in the cell directly in front of the agent (where USE would apply)\n    target_dx, target_dy = DIR_VEC[curr_dir]\n    target_px, target_py = curr_x + target_dx, curr_y + target_dy\n\n    if (0 <= target_px < grid_width and 0 <= target_py < grid_height and\n        grid[target_px, target_py, primitive] == 1):\n      # Found the primitive in front of the agent!\n      # Store this state as the one just before the 'USE' action, and break the BFS.\n      goal_reached_state = (curr_x, curr_y, curr_dir)\n      break\n\n    # Explore possible next movement actions\n    for action in [ACTION_UP, ACTION_RIGHT, ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_LEFT]:\n      # Determine the new position and direction after this action\n      move_dx, move_dy = DIR_VEC[ACTION_TO_DIR[action]]\n      next_x, next_y = curr_x + move_dx, curr_y + move_dy\n      next_dir = ACTION_TO_DIR[action] # Agent faces the direction of its last movement\n\n      # If the next cell is walkable and this (position, direction) state hasn't been visited\n      if is_walkable(next_x, next_y) and (next_x, next_y, next_dir) not in visited:\n        visited.add((next_x, next_y, next_dir))\n        queue.append((next_x, next_y, next_dir))\n        # Store how we reached this new state for path reconstruction.\n        parent_map[(next_x, next_y, next_dir)] = ((curr_x, curr_y, curr_dir), action)\n\n  # If the BFS completes and no path to collect the primitive is found, return an empty list.\n  if goal_reached_state is None:\n    return []\n\n  # Path Reconstruction:\n  # Start with the final 'USE' action.\n  path = [ACTION_USE]\n  # Backtrack from the state from which the 'USE' action was performed.\n  current_path_state = goal_reached_state\n\n  # Reconstruct the path by traversing back through the parent_map until the start state is reached.\n  while current_path_state != (start_x, start_y, start_dir):\n    # Retrieve the parent state and the action taken from that parent to reach current_path_state.\n    parent_state, action_from_parent = parent_map[current_path_state]\n\n    # Prepend the action to the path list (since we are building it backwards).\n    path.insert(0, action_from_parent)\n\n    # Move to the parent state for the next iteration of backtracking.\n    current_path_state = parent_state\n\n  return path", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:06:26.841106", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    # Helper functions for simulating CraftState transitions\n    # These assume that UP/DOWN/LEFT/RIGHT actions are relative to the agent's\n    # current direction, where UP moves forward, DOWN moves backward,\n    # and LEFT/RIGHT are turns. This interpretation is common in grid worlds\n    # and allows for full maneuverability needed for collection.\n    def _simulate_move_forward(pos, direction):\n        r, c = pos\n        if direction == 0:  # North\n            return (r - 1, c)\n        if direction == 1:  # East\n            return (r, c + 1)\n        if direction == 2:  # South\n            return (r + 1, c)\n        if direction == 3:  # West\n            return (r, c - 1)\n        return pos  # Should not happen\n\n    def _simulate_move_backward(pos, direction):\n        r, c = pos\n        if direction == 0:  # North (moving backward is South)\n            return (r + 1, c)\n        if direction == 1:  # East (moving backward is West)\n            return (r, c - 1)\n        if direction == 2:  # South (moving backward is North)\n            return (r - 1, c)\n        if direction == 3:  # West (moving backward is East)\n            return (r, c + 1)\n        return pos  # Should not happen\n\n    def _simulate_turn_left(direction):\n        return (direction - 1 + 4) % 4  # Ensure positive result\n\n    def _simulate_turn_right(direction):\n        return (direction + 1) % 4\n\n    def _is_valid_pos(pos, grid_shape):\n        r, c = pos\n        return 0 <= r < grid_shape[0] and 0 <= c < grid_shape[1]\n\n    # Access the ACTIONS enum from env_factory as it's assumed to be imported.\n    ACTIONS = env_factory.ACTIONS\n\n    # Get initial state information from the environment\n    initial_state = env._current_state\n    initial_grid = initial_state.grid\n    initial_pos = initial_state.pos\n    initial_dir = initial_state.dir\n    world = env.world  # This is the CraftWorld instance\n\n    N_ROWS, N_COLS, _ = initial_grid.shape\n\n    # Pre-check: If the primitive is not grabbable, it cannot be collected.\n    if primitive not in world.grabbable_indices:\n        return []\n\n    # BFS Initialization\n    # Queue stores tuples of (current_position, current_direction, list_of_actions_taken)\n    queue = collections.deque([(initial_pos, initial_dir, [])])\n    # Visited set stores (position, direction) tuples to avoid redundant exploration and cycles\n    visited = set([(initial_pos, initial_dir)])\n\n    while queue:\n        current_pos, current_dir, path_actions = queue.popleft()\n\n        # Check if the agent is currently in a state to collect the primitive\n        # (i.e., the primitive is in the cell directly in front and accessible via USE action)\n        forward_pos = _simulate_move_forward(current_pos, current_dir)\n        if _is_valid_pos(forward_pos, (N_ROWS, N_COLS)):\n            if initial_grid[forward_pos[0], forward_pos[1], primitive] == 1:\n                # Goal reached: primitive is in front. Add the USE action and return the full path.\n                return path_actions + [ACTIONS.USE]\n\n        # Explore possible next actions (movement and turning)\n        # 1. Move Forward (ACTIONS.UP)\n        new_pos_up = _simulate_move_forward(current_pos, current_dir)\n        if _is_valid_pos(new_pos_up, (N_ROWS, N_COLS)) and \\\n           (new_pos_up, current_dir) not in visited:\n            visited.add((new_pos_up, current_dir))\n            queue.append((new_pos_up, current_dir, path_actions + [ACTIONS.UP]))\n\n        # 2. Move Backward (ACTIONS.DOWN)\n        new_pos_down = _simulate_move_backward(current_pos, current_dir)\n        if _is_valid_pos(new_pos_down, (N_ROWS, N_COLS)) and \\\n           (new_pos_down, current_dir) not in visited:\n            visited.add((new_pos_down, current_dir))\n            queue.append((new_pos_down, current_dir, path_actions + [ACTIONS.DOWN]))\n\n        # 3. Turn Left (ACTIONS.LEFT)\n        new_dir_left = _simulate_turn_left(current_dir)\n        if (current_pos, new_dir_left) not in visited:\n            visited.add((current_pos, new_dir_left))\n            queue.append((current_pos, new_dir_left, path_actions + [ACTIONS.LEFT]))\n\n        # 4. Turn Right (ACTIONS.RIGHT)\n        new_dir_right = _simulate_turn_right(current_dir)\n        if (current_pos, new_dir_right) not in visited:\n            visited.add((current_pos, new_dir_right))\n            queue.append((current_pos, new_dir_right, path_actions + [ACTIONS.RIGHT]))\n\n    # If the queue is exhausted and no path to collect the primitive is found\n    return []", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:06:26.913303", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    from collections import deque\n    import numpy as np\n\n    # Constants for directions (assuming standard N, E, S, W mapping for agent's facing direction)\n    # These are internal to the function for clarity, derived from expected action semantics.\n    _NORTH_DIR = 0\n    _EAST_DIR = 1\n    _SOUTH_DIR = 2\n    _WEST_DIR = 3\n\n    # Deltas for each direction (row_change, col_change)\n    _DIR_TO_DELTA = {\n        _NORTH_DIR: (-1, 0),\n        _EAST_DIR: (0, 1),\n        _SOUTH_DIR: (1, 0),\n        _WEST_DIR: (0, -1)\n    }\n\n    # Map movement actions to the direction the agent will be facing AFTER the move\n    # Based on the assumption that UP moves North and sets dir to North_DIR, etc.\n    _ACTION_TO_RESULTING_DIR = {\n        env_factory.UP: _NORTH_DIR,\n        env_factory.RIGHT: _EAST_DIR,\n        env_factory.DOWN: _SOUTH_DIR,\n        env_factory.LEFT: _WEST_DIR\n    }\n\n    _MOVE_ACTIONS = [\n        env_factory.UP,\n        env_factory.RIGHT,\n        env_factory.DOWN,\n        env_factory.LEFT\n    ]\n\n    def _is_cell_passable(r, c, grid_data, non_grabbable_indices, height, width):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a cell is within bounds and does not contain non-grabbable items.\"\"\"\n        if not (0 <= r < height and 0 <= c < width):\n            return False\n        # A cell is not passable if it contains any non-grabbable item\n        for idx in non_grabbable_indices:\n            if grid_data[r, c, idx] == 1: # Assuming 1 indicates presence\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    # 1. Get initial state information from the environment\n    current_state = env._current_state\n    initial_grid = current_state.grid\n    initial_pos = current_state.pos\n    initial_dir = current_state.dir\n    initial_inventory = current_state.inventory\n    world = env.world\n    non_grabbable_indices = world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n    HEIGHT, WIDTH, _ = initial_grid.shape # Extract grid dimensions\n\n    # 2. Pre-check: If the primitive is already in inventory, no actions are needed.\n    if initial_inventory[primitive] > 0:\n        return []\n\n    # 3. Pre-compute a grid indicating which cells are passable (not containing non-grabbable items)\n    is_passable_grid = np.zeros((HEIGHT, WIDTH), dtype=bool)\n    for r in range(HEIGHT):\n        for c in range(WIDTH):\n            is_passable_grid[r, c] = _is_cell_passable(r, c, initial_grid, non_grabbable_indices, HEIGHT, WIDTH)\n\n    # 4. Identify all locations where the primitive exists on the grid.\n    primitive_locations = []\n    for r in range(HEIGHT):\n        for c in range(WIDTH):\n            if initial_grid[r, c, primitive] == 1:\n                primitive_locations.append((r, c))\n\n    if not primitive_locations:\n        # If the primitive is not found anywhere on the grid, it cannot be collected.\n        return []\n\n    # 5. Define goal states for BFS: (agent_row, agent_col, agent_direction)\n    # A goal state means the agent is positioned such that the primitive is in the square directly in front of it.\n    goal_states = set() \n    for pr, pc in primitive_locations: # (pr, pc) is the location of the primitive\n        for target_dir, (dr, dc) in _DIR_TO_DELTA.items(): # Iterate through all possible facing directions\n            # Calculate the cell (agent_r, agent_c) where the agent must stand\n            # so that when facing 'target_dir', it looks at (pr, pc).\n            # The relationship is: (pr, pc) = (agent_r + dr, agent_c + dc)\n            # Therefore: (agent_r, agent_c) = (pr - dr, pc - dc)\n            agent_r = pr - dr\n            agent_c = pc - dc\n            \n            # Check if this calculated agent position is within bounds and passable.\n            # Using the precomputed `is_passable_grid` for efficiency and correctness.\n            if 0 <= agent_r < HEIGHT and 0 <= agent_c < WIDTH and is_passable_grid[agent_r, agent_c]:\n                goal_states.add((agent_r, agent_c, target_dir))\n\n    if not goal_states:\n        # If no reachable spots next to a primitive with correct orientation, return empty.\n        return []\n\n    # 6. Perform a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path to a goal state.\n    # The queue stores tuples: ((current_row, current_col, current_dir), [actions_taken_so_far])\n    queue = deque([((initial_pos[0], initial_pos[1], initial_dir), [])])\n    # The visited set stores (row, col, dir) to prevent cycles and redundant explorations.\n    visited = set([(initial_pos[0], initial_pos[1], initial_dir)])\n\n    while queue:\n        (r, c, d), path = queue.popleft()\n\n        # Check if the current state (position and direction) is one of our defined goal states.\n        if (r, c, d) in goal_states:\n            # If a goal state is reached, append the 'USE' action and return the full path.\n            return path + [env_factory.USE]\n\n        # Explore possible next states by applying valid movement actions.\n        for move_action in _MOVE_ACTIONS:\n            next_dir = _ACTION_TO_RESULTING_DIR[move_action] # Direction agent will face after this move\n            dr, dc = _DIR_TO_DELTA[next_dir] # Delta corresponding to the new direction for movement\n\n            # Calculate the new position after performing the move action.\n            next_r, next_c = r + dr, c + dc\n\n            # Check if the new cell is within bounds and is passable.\n            if 0 <= next_r < HEIGHT and 0 <= next_c < WIDTH and is_passable_grid[next_r, next_c]:\n                next_state = (next_r, next_c, next_dir)\n                if next_state not in visited:\n                    visited.add(next_state)\n                    queue.append((next_state, path + [move_action]))\n\n    # If the BFS completes and the queue is exhausted without finding any path to a goal state,\n    # return an empty list indicating that the primitive cannot be collected.\n    return []", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:08:35.318099", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    total_actions = []\n    \n    # Max actions to prevent infinite loops or excessively long paths\n    MAX_TOTAL_ACTIONS = 200 \n\n    # Action mappings (from CraftLab.action_specs)\n    ACTION_DOWN = 0\n    ACTION_UP = 1\n    ACTION_LEFT = 2\n    ACTION_RIGHT = 3\n    ACTION_USE = 4\n\n    # Direction mappings (from CraftState description)\n    DIR_UP = 0\n    DIR_RIGHT = 1\n    DIR_DOWN = 2\n    DIR_LEFT = 3\n\n    # Helper for direction to (dx, dy) representing (change in x/column, change in y/row)\n    DIR_TO_DXDY = {\n        DIR_UP: (0, -1),\n        DIR_RIGHT: (1, 0),\n        DIR_DOWN: (0, 1),\n        DIR_LEFT: (-1, 0),\n    }\n    # Helper for (dx, dy) to direction\n    DXDY_TO_DIR = {v: k for k, v in DIR_TO_DXDY.items()}\n\n    # Loop until the primitive is collected or max actions reached\n    # This outer loop allows re-evaluating the state after a path is executed\n    # in case the environment changes unexpectedly or the USE action succeeds.\n    for _ in range(MAX_TOTAL_ACTIONS): \n        state = env._current_state # Get current CraftState\n\n        # 1. Check if primitive is already in inventory\n        if state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n            return total_actions\n\n        start_pos = state.pos\n        WIDTH, HEIGHT, N_KINDS = state.grid.shape\n\n        # BFS to find the closest cell adjacent to the primitive\n        # Node in queue: (current_pos, list_of_actions_to_reach_current_pos)\n        bfs_queue = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) \n        bfs_visited = {start_pos} # Set of visited positions\n\n        # (dx, dy, action_to_perform_to_move_in_that_direction)\n        move_deltas_with_actions = [\n            (0, -1, ACTION_UP),    # Move UP: (0, -1) delta, action UP\n            (0, 1, ACTION_DOWN),   # Move DOWN: (0, 1) delta, action DOWN\n            (-1, 0, ACTION_LEFT),  # Move LEFT: (-1, 0) delta, action LEFT\n            (1, 0, ACTION_RIGHT),  # Move RIGHT: (1, 0) delta, action RIGHT\n        ]\n        \n        found_path_info = None # Stores (path_to_adj_pos, adj_pos, primitive_pos_on_grid)\n\n        while bfs_queue:\n            current_pos, path_to_current = bfs_queue.popleft()\n            cx, cy = current_pos\n\n            # Check if any neighbor of current_pos contains the primitive\n            for dx, dy, _ in move_deltas_with_actions: \n                nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy\n                if 0 <= nx < WIDTH and 0 <= ny < HEIGHT:\n                    # If neighbor cell (nx, ny) contains the primitive\n                    if state.grid[nx, ny, primitive] > 0:\n                        # We found a target: current_pos is adjacent to (nx, ny) which has the primitive.\n                        # So, current_pos is the \"adjacent position\" from which we will USE.\n                        found_path_info = (path_to_current, current_pos, (nx, ny))\n                        break # Found the shortest path to an adjacent cell, exit inner loop\n            if found_path_info:\n                break # Exit BFS queue loop\n\n            # Explore neighbors for movement\n            for dx, dy, action_to_take in move_deltas_with_actions:\n                next_x, next_y = cx + dx, cy + dy\n                next_pos = (next_x, next_y)\n\n                # Check bounds\n                if not (0 <= next_x < WIDTH and not (0 <= next_y < HEIGHT)): # Fixed typo in condition\n                    continue\n\n                # Check if already visited\n                if next_pos in bfs_visited:\n                    continue\n\n                # Check for obstacles (non-grabbable items or the primitive itself)\n                is_blocked = False\n                for k_idx in range(N_KINDS):\n                    # If there's content at next_pos\n                    if state.grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx] > 0:\n                        # If it's the primitive we are looking for, we cannot step on it.\n                        # Or if it's a non-grabbable item (obstacle).\n                        if k_idx == primitive or k_idx in state.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n                            is_blocked = True\n                            break\n                if is_blocked:\n                    continue\n                \n                # If not blocked and not visited, add to queue\n                bfs_visited.add(next_pos)\n                bfs_queue.append((next_pos, path_to_current + [action_to_take]))\n\n        if not found_path_info:\n            # Primitive is not found or unreachable from the current position.\n            # This can happen if the primitive is behind walls, or simply not present on grid.\n            return total_actions # Return what we have (could be empty)\n\n        # Execute the path found by BFS\n        path_to_adj_pos, adj_pos, primitive_pos_on_grid = found_path_info\n        \n        # 2. First, execute the movement actions to reach the position adjacent to the primitive\n        for action in path_to_adj_pos:\n            if len(total_actions) >= MAX_TOTAL_ACTIONS:\n                return total_actions # Safety break if path is too long\n            _, _, _ = env.step(action)\n            total_actions.append(action)\n            state = env._current_state # Update state after each action\n            if state.inventory[primitive] > 0: # Check if collected somehow during movement (unlikely, but safe)\n                return total_actions\n\n        # 3. Now agent is at adj_pos. Need to turn to face the primitive and then USE.\n        agent_x, agent_y = state.pos \n        prim_x, prim_y = primitive_pos_on_grid\n\n        # Calculate required direction to face the primitive\n        target_dx = prim_x - agent_x\n        target_dy = prim_y - agent_y\n        required_dir = DXDY_TO_DIR.get((target_dx, target_dy))\n\n        if required_dir is not None: # Should always be found if primitive_pos_on_grid is valid neighbor\n            current_dir = state.dir\n            \n            # Calculate minimum turns (left or right)\n            turns_left = (current_dir - required_dir + 4) % 4\n            turns_right = (required_dir - current_dir + 4) % 4\n\n            # Execute turns\n            if turns_left <= turns_right: # Prioritize left turns or equal turns\n                for _ in range(turns_left):\n                    if len(total_actions) >= MAX_TOTAL_ACTIONS: return total_actions\n                    _, _, _ = env.step(ACTION_LEFT)\n                    total_actions.append(ACTION_LEFT)\n                    state = env._current_state # Update state after turning\n            else:\n                for _ in range(turns_right):\n                    if len(total_actions) >= MAX_TOTAL_ACTIONS: return total_actions\n                    _, _, _ = env.step(ACTION_RIGHT)\n                    total_actions.append(ACTION_RIGHT)\n                    state = env._current_state # Update state after turning\n\n            # 4. Finally, USE the primitive\n            if len(total_actions) >= MAX_TOTAL_ACTIONS: return total_actions\n            _, _, _ = env.step(ACTION_USE)\n            total_actions.append(ACTION_USE)\n            state = env._current_state # Update state after USE\n\n            # The outer loop will re-check the inventory in the next iteration.\n            # If the USE was successful, it will return total_actions.\n\n    # If MAX_TOTAL_ACTIONS limit is reached without collecting the primitive\n    return total_actions", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:08:35.395750", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    # 1. Initialize action mappings\n    action_map = env.action_specs()\n    ACTION_DOWN = action_map['DOWN']\n    ACTION_UP = action_map['UP']\n    ACTION_LEFT = action_map['LEFT']\n    ACTION_RIGHT = action_map['RIGHT']\n    ACTION_USE = action_map['USE']\n\n    # Movement deltas and corresponding actions/resulting directions\n    # These are relative moves (dx, dy) and the action that causes them.\n    # The direction resulting from the move: 0=N, 1=E, 2=S, 3=W (DMLab standard)\n    MOVES = {\n        (0, -1): ACTION_UP,    # Moving up (y-1) -> Agent faces North (0)\n        (0, +1): ACTION_DOWN,  # Moving down (y+1) -> Agent faces South (2)\n        (-1, 0): ACTION_LEFT,  # Moving left (x-1) -> Agent faces West (3)\n        (+1, 0): ACTION_RIGHT  # Moving right (x+1) -> Agent faces East (1)\n    }\n\n    # Map the (dx, dy) of a move to the resulting direction code.\n    # This assumes the agent faces the direction it just moved.\n    MOVE_DELTA_TO_RESULTING_DIR = {\n        (0, -1): 0, # North\n        (0, 1): 2,  # South\n        (-1, 0): 3, # West\n        (1, 0): 1   # East\n    }\n    \n    # Map direction codes to their corresponding (dx, dy) vectors (e.g., for USE action target)\n    DIR_CODE_TO_DELTA = {\n        0: (0, -1), # North\n        1: (1, 0),  # East\n        2: (0, 1),  # South\n        3: (-1, 0)  # West\n    }\n\n    # 2. Get current CraftState info\n    state = env._current_state\n    grid = state.grid\n    current_pos_x, current_pos_y = state.pos\n    current_dir = state.dir # Initial direction\n    \n    W, H, n_kinds = grid.shape\n\n    # Identify non-grabbable items that act as obstacles for movement.\n    obstacle_kinds = state.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n    def is_walkable(x, y):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a cell (x, y) is within bounds and not occupied by an obstacle.\"\"\"\n        if not (0 <= x < W and 0 <= y < H):\n            return False\n        \n        # Check if any obstacle kind is present at this cell\n        for kind_idx in obstacle_kinds:\n            # If an obstacle is present AND it's not the primitive we're looking for (which shouldn't be an obstacle)\n            if grid[x, y, kind_idx] > 0 and kind_idx != primitive:\n                return False # It's an obstacle\n        return True\n\n    # 3. Find all primitive locations on the grid\n    primitive_locations = []\n    for x in range(W):\n        for y in range(H):\n            if grid[x, y, primitive] > 0:\n                primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n    if not primitive_locations:\n        return [] # Primitive not found, cannot collect\n\n    # 4. Prepare potential target \"pickup spots\" for BFS\n    # A target is a tuple: ((agent_x, agent_y), required_agent_dir_to_face_primitive)\n    # The agent needs to stand at (agent_x, agent_y) and face `required_agent_dir_to_face_primitive`\n    # such that the primitive at (px, py) is directly in front of it.\n    \n    target_pickup_spots = set() \n    for px, py in primitive_locations:\n        # Iterate over all 4 cardinal directions (vectors from agent to primitive)\n        for dx, dy in DIR_CODE_TO_DELTA.values(): \n            # Calculate the required agent position (ax, ay) given (px, py) and (dx, dy)\n            # If agent at (ax,ay) and primitive at (px,py), then (px-ax, py-ay) = (dx,dy)\n            # So, (ax, ay) = (px - dx, py - dy).\n            \n            target_agent_pos_x = px - dx\n            target_agent_pos_y = py - dy\n            \n            # Check if this potential agent position is walkable\n            if not is_walkable(target_agent_pos_x, target_agent_pos_y):\n                continue\n            \n            # The required direction for the agent to face at (target_agent_pos_x, target_agent_pos_y)\n            # is the direction corresponding to the vector (dx, dy).\n            # This is a direct lookup from MOVE_DELTA_TO_RESULTING_DIR mapping move vectors to dir codes.\n            required_facing_dir = MOVE_DELTA_TO_RESULTING_DIR[(dx, dy)]\n            \n            target_pickup_spots.add(((target_agent_pos_x, target_agent_pos_y), required_facing_dir))\n\n    if not target_pickup_spots:\n        # This could happen if all primitive locations are surrounded by non-walkable obstacles\n        return []\n\n    # 5. BFS for shortest path\n    q = collections.deque()\n    # State in queue: ((current_x, current_y, current_dir_code), path_list_of_actions)\n    \n    # Visited set to prevent cycles and re-exploring worse paths\n    # State in visited: (x, y, dir_code)\n    visited = set()\n\n    # Initial state (agent's start position and direction)\n    q.append(((current_pos_x, current_pos_y, current_dir), []))\n    visited.add((current_pos_x, current_pos_y, current_dir))\n\n    while q:\n        (cx, cy, c_dir), path = q.popleft()\n\n        # Check if current state (position and direction) is a target pickup spot\n        # If the agent arrives at (cx,cy) and its last move implicitly set its direction to c_dir,\n        # AND this (cx,cy,c_dir) matches one of our target_pickup_spots, we are done.\n        if ((cx, cy), c_dir) in target_pickup_spots:\n            return path + [ACTION_USE]\n\n        # Explore possible moves from current state\n        # (move_delta_x, move_delta_y) represents the movement vector\n        for move_delta, action_val in MOVES.items():\n            nx, ny = cx + move_delta[0], cy + move_delta[1]\n\n            # Check if new position is walkable\n            if not is_walkable(nx, ny):\n                continue\n            \n            # The new direction is determined by the move action taken to reach (nx, ny)\n            n_dir = MOVE_DELTA_TO_RESULTING_DIR[move_delta]\n            \n            # If this state (position and direction) has not been visited before\n            if (nx, ny, n_dir) not in visited:\n                visited.add((nx, ny, n_dir))\n                q.append(((nx, ny, n_dir), path + [action_val]))\n                \n    # If no path found to any target pickup spot\n    return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:10:00.001207", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    state = env._current_state\n\n    # 1. Check if primitive is already in inventory\n    if state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n        return []\n\n    # 2. Get action mappings from the environment\n    actions_map = env.action_specs()\n    ACTION_UP = actions_map['UP']\n    ACTION_DOWN = actions_map['DOWN']\n    ACTION_LEFT = actions_map['LEFT']\n    ACTION_RIGHT = actions_map['RIGHT']\n    ACTION_USE = actions_map['USE']\n\n    # 3. Define movement/direction deltas based on a common DMLab-like interpretation:\n    # UP/DOWN are move forward/backward relative to agent's direction.\n    # LEFT/RIGHT are turn actions.\n    # DR/DC for dir: 0 (North: row-1), 1 (East: col+1), 2 (South: row+1), 3 (West: col-1)\n    DR = [-1, 0, 1, 0] \n    DC = [0, 1, 0, -1] \n\n    # 4. Get grid dimensions and kinds that block movement\n    grid_rows, grid_cols = state.grid.shape[:2]\n    # Cells containing these kinds cannot be moved into\n    blocked_kinds = env.world.non_grabbable_indices.union(env.world.workshop_indices)\n\n    # Helper function to check if a cell is traversable\n    def is_traversable(r, c):\n        # Check bounds\n        if not (0 <= r < grid_rows and 0 <= c < grid_cols):\n            return False\n        # Check if cell contains any blocking kind\n        for k_idx in blocked_kinds:\n            if state.grid[r, c, k_idx] > 0:\n                return False # Cell contains a non-traversable item\n        return True\n\n    # 5. BFS for pathfinding\n    # Queue stores tuples: ((current_row, current_col, current_direction), path_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n    queue = collections.deque([((state.pos[0], state.pos[1], state.dir), [])])\n    \n    # Visited set stores (row, col, direction) tuples to avoid cycles and redundant paths\n    visited = set([(state.pos[0], state.pos[1], state.dir)])\n    \n    final_actions = []\n\n    while queue:\n        (r, c, d), path_so_far = queue.popleft()\n\n        # Check if primitive is directly in front and can be USED\n        pr, pc = r + DR[d], c + DC[d] # Cell in front of the agent\n        if (0 <= pr < grid_rows and 0 <= pc < grid_cols and\n                state.grid[pr, pc, primitive] > 0):\n            final_actions = path_so_far + [ACTION_USE]\n            break # Found the shortest path to collect the primitive\n\n        # Explore possible actions from the current state (r, c, d)\n\n        # Action: Move Forward (UP)\n        nr_f, nc_f = r + DR[d], c + DC[d] # New position after moving forward\n        nd_f = d # Direction remains unchanged after movement\n        if is_traversable(nr_f, nc_f) and (nr_f, nc_f, nd_f) not in visited:\n            visited.add((nr_f, nc_f, nd_f))\n            queue.append(((nr_f, nc_f, nd_f), path_so_far + [ACTION_UP]))\n\n        # Action: Move Backward (DOWN)\n        nr_b, nc_b = r - DR[d], c - DC[d] # New position after moving backward\n        nd_b = d # Direction remains unchanged after movement\n        if is_traversable(nr_b, nc_b) and (nr_b, nc_b, nd_b) not in visited:\n            visited.add((nr_b, nc_b, nd_b))\n            queue.append(((nr_b, nc_b, nd_b), path_so_far + [ACTION_DOWN]))\n\n        # Action: Turn Left (LEFT)\n        nr_l, nc_l = r, c # Position remains unchanged after turning\n        nd_l = (d - 1 + 4) % 4 # New direction (cyclical: 0->3, 1->0, etc.)\n        if (nr_l, nc_l, nd_l) not in visited:\n            visited.add((nr_l, nc_l, nd_l))\n            queue.append(((nr_l, nc_l, nd_l), path_so_far + [ACTION_LEFT]))\n\n        # Action: Turn Right (RIGHT)\n        nr_r, nc_r = r, c # Position remains unchanged after turning\n        nd_r = (d + 1) % 4 # New direction (cyclical: 0->1, 1->2, etc.)\n        if (nr_r, nc_r, nd_r) not in visited:\n            visited.add((nr_r, nc_r, nd_r))\n            queue.append(((nr_r, nc_r, nd_r), path_so_far + [ACTION_RIGHT]))\n            \n    return final_actions", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:10:01.031311", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  initial_state = env._current_state\n\n  # If the primitive is already in inventory, no actions needed.\n  if initial_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Define all possible actions: DOWN=0, UP=1, LEFT=2, RIGHT=3, USE=4\n  ALL_ACTIONS = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]\n\n  # Queue for BFS: stores (CraftState object, list of actions to reach this state)\n  # collections.deque is assumed to be available.\n  queue = collections.deque([(initial_state, [])])\n\n  # Set to keep track of visited states to prevent cycles and redundant explorations.\n  # A state is defined by (agent_x_position, agent_y_position, agent_direction, tuple_of_inventory_counts).\n  # numpy is assumed to be available for initial_state.inventory.\n  visited = set()\n  initial_state_key = (initial_state.pos[0], initial_state.pos[1], initial_state.dir, tuple(initial_state.inventory))\n  visited.add(initial_state_key)\n\n  # A safety limit to prevent excessive computation in very large or unsolvable environments.\n  # This value might need tuning depending on grid size and complexity.\n  MAX_EXPLORED_STATES = 50000 \n\n  while queue:\n    current_state, current_path = queue.popleft()\n\n    # If the primitive has been collected in the current state, we found a path.\n    if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n      return current_path\n\n    # If we've explored too many unique states without finding a solution,\n    # it's likely unreachable within reasonable limits.\n    if len(visited) >= MAX_EXPLORED_STATES:\n      return [] # Indicate no path found within limits\n\n    # Explore all possible actions from the current state\n    for action in ALL_ACTIONS:\n      # Simulate the action to get the next state\n      # CraftState.step returns (reward, new_state)\n      _, new_state = current_state.step(action)\n\n      # Create a hashable key for the new state\n      new_state_key = (new_state.pos[0], new_state.pos[1], new_state.dir, tuple(new_state.inventory))\n\n      # If this new state has not been visited before, add it to the queue\n      if new_state_key not in visited:\n        visited.add(new_state_key)\n        queue.append((new_state, current_path + [action]))\n\n  # If the queue becomes empty and the goal was not reached, it means\n  # the primitive is unreachable from the initial state.\n  return []", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:10:59.084819", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    # Start by getting the initial CraftState instance from the CraftLab environment.\n    initial_craft_state = env._current_state\n\n    # If the primitive is already in the inventory, no actions are needed.\n    if initial_craft_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Use a deque for BFS to store (CraftState, list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state).\n    # 'collections' must be imported at the top level of the file.\n    q = collections.deque()\n    q.append((initial_craft_state, []))\n\n    # Use a set to keep track of visited states to avoid cycles and redundant computations.\n    # A state is defined by its grid layout, agent's position, direction, and inventory.\n    # 'numpy' must be imported as np at the top level of the file for .tobytes().\n    visited = set()\n    initial_state_hash = (\n        initial_craft_state.grid.tobytes(),\n        initial_craft_state.pos,\n        initial_craft_state.dir,\n        initial_craft_state.inventory.tobytes()\n    )\n    visited.add(initial_state_hash)\n\n    # Set a maximum search depth to prevent infinite loops in complex or unreachable scenarios.\n    # This helps ensure the function completes in a reasonable time.\n    MAX_SEARCH_DEPTH = 250\n\n    # Action constants (assuming env_factory is imported and defines these integers).\n    # These constants are typically defined globally or imported from env_factory.\n    DOWN = env_factory.DOWN\n    UP = env_factory.UP\n    LEFT = env_factory.LEFT\n    RIGHT = env_factory.RIGHT\n    USE = env_factory.USE\n\n    while q:\n        current_state, current_path = q.popleft()\n\n        # If the path length exceeds the maximum search depth, stop exploring this path.\n        if len(current_path) >= MAX_SEARCH_DEPTH:\n            continue\n\n        # Explore all possible actions from the current state.\n        for action in [DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT, USE]:\n            # Simulate the action. CraftState.step returns a *new* CraftState instance,\n            # which is crucial for BFS as it avoids modifying the original state.\n            _reward, next_state = current_state.step(action)\n\n            # Check if the primitive has been collected in the new state.\n            if next_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n                # Goal achieved! Return the path including the current action.\n                return current_path + [action]\n\n            # Create a hashable representation of the next state for the visited set.\n            next_state_hash = (\n                next_state.grid.tobytes(),\n                next_state.pos,\n                next_state.dir,\n                next_state.inventory.tobytes()\n            )\n\n            # If this state has not been visited before, add it to the queue and visited set.\n            if next_state_hash not in visited:\n                visited.add(next_state_hash)\n                q.append((next_state, current_path + [action]))\n\n    # If the queue becomes empty and the primitive has not been collected,\n    # it means the primitive is unreachable from the initial state within the search limits.\n    return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:10:59.154593", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    # Action constants (refer to CraftLab.action_specs for mapping)\n    DOWN = 0\n    UP = 1\n    LEFT = 2\n    RIGHT = 3\n    USE = 4\n\n    # Map movement actions to coordinate changes (row_delta, col_delta)\n    DELTAS = {\n        UP: (-1, 0),\n        DOWN: (1, 0),\n        LEFT: (0, -1),\n        RIGHT: (0, 1)\n    }\n\n    current_state = env._current_state\n    \n    # 1. Check if the primitive is already in inventory\n    if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n        return []\n\n    # 2. Perform a Breadth-First Search (BFS) to find the shortest path\n    #    to a cell from which the primitive can be 'USE'd (i.e., adjacent to it).\n    \n    # Queue for BFS: stores tuples of ((row, col), list_of_actions_taken)\n    queue = collections.deque() \n    \n    # Set to keep track of visited grid positions to avoid cycles and redundant processing.\n    # Stores (row, col) tuples.\n    visited = set() \n\n    # Initial state for BFS: agent's current position and an empty path\n    initial_pos = current_state.pos\n    queue.append((initial_pos, []))\n    visited.add(initial_pos)\n\n    # Get grid dimensions for boundary checks\n    GRID_HEIGHT, GRID_WIDTH, _ = current_state.grid.shape\n\n    # BFS loop\n    while queue:\n        (r, c), path = queue.popleft()\n\n        # Create a hypothetical CraftState to leverage its `next_to` method.\n        # This allows checking if the current BFS position is adjacent to the primitive\n        # using the existing game logic. We pass current_state's components\n        # (grid, scenario, inventory, etc.) as they are relevant for `next_to`.\n        # Using type(current_state) allows for robustness if current_state is a subclass.\n        hypothetical_state = type(current_state)(\n            scenario=current_state.scenario,\n            grid=current_state.grid,\n            pos=(r, c),\n            dir=current_state.dir, # Direction doesn't impact next_to or basic movement checks\n            inventory=current_state.inventory # Inventory doesn't change during pathfinding\n        )\n\n        # Check if the current hypothetical position is adjacent to the primitive.\n        # If it is, we've found the shortest path to a suitable 'USE' location.\n        if hypothetical_state.next_to(primitive):\n            # Append the 'USE' action and return the complete action sequence.\n            return path + [USE]\n\n        # Explore all possible movement actions (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT) from the current position\n        for action, (dr, dc) in DELTAS.items():\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n\n            # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries\n            if 0 <= nr < GRID_HEIGHT and 0 <= nc < GRID_WIDTH:\n                # If this new position has not been visited yet, add it to the queue\n                if (nr, nc) not in visited:\n                    visited.add((nr, nc))\n                    new_path = path + [action]\n                    queue.append(((nr, nc), new_path))\n    \n    # If the BFS queue becomes empty and no path to the primitive was found,\n    # it means the primitive is unreachable or not present on the map.\n    return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:13:10.246088", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  actions_list = []\n\n  # 1. Get Initial State from current environment observation\n  obs = env.observations()\n\n  # Check if primitive is already in inventory\n  inventory = obs['features_dict']['inventory']\n  if inventory[primitive] > 0:\n    return [] # Already collected, no actions needed\n\n  current_grid = obs['features_dict']['features_global']\n  current_pos_norm = obs['features_dict']['pos']\n\n  # Grid dimensions (height, width, kinds)\n  # numpy indexing is typically (row, column), so (y, x)\n  height, width, _ = current_grid.shape \n  \n  # Convert normalized position to grid coordinates (x, y)\n  # The normalization is typically (value / (DIMENSION - 1))\n  current_pos_x = int(round(current_pos_norm[0] * (width - 1)))\n  current_pos_y = int(round(current_pos_norm[1] * (height - 1)))\n  current_pos = (current_pos_x, current_pos_y)\n\n  # 2. Locate all primitive instances on the grid\n  primitive_locations = []\n  for y in range(height):\n    for x in range(width):\n      # Check if the primitive kind exists at this (x, y) cell\n      if current_grid[y, x, primitive] > 0:\n        primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n  if not primitive_locations:\n    # Primitive not found anywhere on the map\n    return []\n\n  # 3. Find the closest target adjacent position to any primitive\n  #    This is the cell the agent needs to move to before using the primitive.\n  min_dist = float('inf')\n  target_adjacent_pos = None\n  \n  # Iterate through all primitive locations\n  for px, py in primitive_locations:\n    # Check all 4 direct (non-diagonal) adjacent cells around the primitive\n    # (0,1) is down, (0,-1) is up, (1,0) is right, (-1,0) is left relative to the primitive\n    for dx, dy in [(0, 1), (0, -1), (1, 0), (-1, 0)]:\n      adj_x, adj_y = px + dx, py + dy\n      \n      # Check if the adjacent cell is within grid boundaries\n      if 0 <= adj_x < width and 0 <= adj_y < height:\n        # Calculate Manhattan distance from the agent's current position to this adjacent cell\n        dist = abs(adj_x - current_pos[0]) + abs(adj_y - current_pos[1])\n        \n        # If this adjacent cell is closer, update our target\n        if dist < min_dist:\n          min_dist = dist\n          target_adjacent_pos = (adj_x, adj_y)\n\n  if target_adjacent_pos is None:\n    # This case should ideally not be reached if primitive_locations is not empty\n    # and the grid has at least one valid adjacent cell for any primitive.\n    return []\n\n  # 4. Pathfinding using Breadth-First Search (BFS) to reach target_adjacent_pos\n  # Queue stores tuples of (current_position, list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n  # collections.deque is used for efficient queue operations\n  queue = collections.deque([(current_pos, [])])\n  # Set to keep track of visited positions to avoid cycles and redundant paths\n  visited = {current_pos}\n  \n  path_found = False\n  \n  while queue:\n    (r_x, r_y), path = queue.popleft()\n\n    # If we reached the target adjacent position, we found the shortest path\n    if (r_x, r_y) == target_adjacent_pos:\n      actions_list.extend(path)\n      path_found = True\n      break # Path found, no need to explore further\n    \n    # Explore neighbors by trying all possible movement actions\n    for action, (dx, dy) in ACTION_DELTAS.items():\n      new_x, new_y = r_x + dx, r_y + dy\n      new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n      \n      # Check if the new position is within grid boundaries and has not been visited\n      if 0 <= new_x < width and 0 <= new_y < height and new_pos not in visited:\n        visited.add(new_pos)\n        # Add the new position and the updated path to the queue\n        queue.append((new_pos, path + [action]))\n  \n  if not path_found:\n    # No path could be found to any adjacent cell (e.g., primitive is in an enclosed area)\n    return []\n\n  # 5. After reaching the adjacent position, add the USE action\n  # This assumes that the USE action will succeed if a grabbable primitive is adjacent.\n  # No explicit turning actions are provided in the CraftLab action_specs,\n  # implying USE acts omnidirectionally on adjacent items.\n  actions_list.append(USE)\n  \n  return actions_list", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:13:11.205610", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import numpy as np\n  import collections # For deque\n\n  # Define action constants (assuming these are standard for CraftLab)\n  ACTION_DOWN = 0\n  ACTION_UP = 1\n  ACTION_LEFT = 2\n  ACTION_RIGHT = 3\n  ACTION_USE = 4\n\n  # Define delta (column, row) for each direction (EAST, NORTH, WEST, SOUTH as 0, 1, 2, 3)\n  # Based on CraftState.step() checking grid[self.pos[0] + DR[self.dir], self.pos[1] + DC[self.dir], :]\n  # and assuming pos is (x, y) = (col, row)\n  # So DR corresponds to delta_y (row change), DC corresponds to delta_x (col change)\n  # 0: EAST (x+1, y) -> (col+1, row)\n  # 1: NORTH (x, y-1) -> (col, row-1)\n  # 2: WEST (x-1, y) -> (col-1, row)\n  # 3: SOUTH (x, y+1) -> (col, row+1)\n  DC_FACE = [1, 0, -1, 0] # Delta Column for facing directions (x-axis change)\n  DR_FACE = [0, -1, 0, 1] # Delta Row for facing directions (y-axis change)\n\n  # Define movement deltas and corresponding actions for BFS\n  # Order: DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT\n  DC_MOVE = [0, 0, -1, 1] # Delta Column for movement (x-axis change)\n  DR_MOVE = [1, -1, 0, 0] # Delta Row for movement (y-axis change)\n  MOVE_ACTIONS = [ACTION_DOWN, ACTION_UP, ACTION_LEFT, ACTION_RIGHT]\n\n  MAX_COLLECT_STEPS = 200 # Max steps to attempt collection\n\n  actions_taken = []\n\n  for _ in range(MAX_COLLECT_STEPS):\n    obs = env.observations()\n\n    # 1. Check if primitive is already in inventory\n    inventory = obs['features_dict']['inventory']\n    if inventory[primitive] > 0:\n      return actions_taken # Goal achieved\n\n    # Get current state information\n    grid = obs['features_dict']['features_global']\n    grid_width, grid_height, _ = grid.shape # grid is (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds), so (cols, rows, kinds)\n\n    # Convert normalized position (x, y) to (col, row) grid coordinates\n    norm_pos = obs['features_dict']['pos']\n    current_col = int(norm_pos[0] * (grid_width - 1))\n    current_row = int(norm_pos[1] * (grid_height - 1))\n    current_dir = obs['features_dict']['direction'].argmax() # One-hot to index\n\n    # 2. Check if primitive is immediately in front and can be USE'd\n    front_col = current_col + DC_FACE[current_dir]\n    front_row = current_row + DR_FACE[current_dir]\n\n    if (0 <= front_col < grid_width and\n        0 <= front_row < grid_height and\n        grid[front_col, front_row, primitive] > 0):\n      # Primitive is in front, USE it\n      _, _, next_obs = env.step(ACTION_USE)\n      actions_taken.append(ACTION_USE)\n      # Update obs for next iteration\n      obs = next_obs\n      continue # Re-evaluate state after USE\n\n    # 3. BFS to find a path to the closest primitive location\n    target_locations = []\n    for c in range(grid_width):\n      for r in range(grid_height):\n        if grid[c, r, primitive] > 0:\n          target_locations.append((c, r))\n\n    if not target_locations:\n      # No primitive found in the world, cannot collect\n      return actions_taken\n\n    q = collections.deque([(current_col, current_row, [])]) # (col, row, path_actions_from_start)\n    visited = set([(current_col, current_row)])\n\n    path_to_target_primitive = None # Stores list of actions to reach the primitive's cell\n    primitive_at_pos = None        # Stores (col, row) of the primitive found\n\n    while q and path_to_target_primitive is None:\n      c, r, path_so_far = q.popleft()\n\n      if (c, r) in target_locations:\n        path_to_target_primitive = path_so_far\n        primitive_at_pos = (c, r)\n        break # Found the closest primitive\n\n      # Explore neighbors for movement\n      for i in range(len(MOVE_ACTIONS)):\n        next_c, next_r = c + DC_MOVE[i], r + DR_MOVE[i]\n        \n        # Check bounds and if already visited\n        if (0 <= next_c < grid_width and\n            0 <= next_r < grid_height and\n            (next_c, next_r) not in visited):\n          \n          # Basic traversability check: avoid cells with non-grabbable items if possible.\n          # For simplicity here, assuming all cells are traversable for pathfinding.\n          # A more robust solution would check `env._current_state.world.non_grabbable_indices`\n          # but that accesses internal state not guaranteed by `env` interface.\n          \n          visited.add((next_c, next_r))\n          q.append((next_c, next_r, path_so_far + [MOVE_ACTIONS[i]]))\n\n    # 4. Execute the determined action\n    if path_to_target_primitive:\n      # Path found, take the first step towards the primitive\n      next_action = path_to_target_primitive[0]\n      _, _, next_obs = env.step(next_action)\n      actions_taken.append(next_action)\n      obs = next_obs # Update obs for next iteration\n    else:\n      # No path found by BFS, or agent is already at the primitive's location (min_dist=0)\n      if primitive_at_pos == (current_col, current_row):\n        # Agent is standing on the primitive. Needs to move off, turn, and USE.\n        # Find an adjacent empty cell to move to.\n        empty_adj_pos = None\n        for i in range(len(MOVE_ACTIONS)):\n          test_c, test_r = current_col + DC_MOVE[i], current_row + DR_MOVE[i]\n          if (0 <= test_c < grid_width and 0 <= test_r < grid_height):\n            # Check if cell is 'empty' (contains no items, or only traversable environment items)\n            # Simplistic check: if sum of all kinds at (test_c, test_r) is 0, it's empty.\n            if np.sum(grid[test_c, test_r, :]) == 0:\n              empty_adj_pos = (test_c, test_r)\n              break\n        \n        if empty_adj_pos:\n          # Move to the empty adjacent cell\n          move_to_empty_c, move_to_empty_r = empty_adj_pos\n          move_action = None\n          if move_to_empty_r > current_row: move_action = ACTION_DOWN\n          elif move_to_empty_r < current_row: move_action = ACTION_UP\n          elif move_to_empty_c > current_col: move_action = ACTION_RIGHT\n          elif move_to_empty_c < current_col: move_action = ACTION_LEFT\n          \n          if move_action is not None:\n            _, _, next_obs = env.step(move_action)\n            actions_taken.append(move_action)\n            obs = next_obs # Update obs for next iteration\n            continue # Re-evaluate state after move\n          else:\n            # Should not happen if empty_adj_pos is truly adjacent\n            return actions_taken # Cannot proceed\n        else:\n          # No empty adjacent cell found, stuck on primitive, cannot move off.\n          return actions_taken # Cannot collect\n\n      else: # No path found and not at primitive - implies primitive is unreachable or pathfinding failed.\n        return actions_taken # Cannot collect\n\n  # If max_collect_steps reached without collecting the primitive\n  return actions_taken", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:15:05.101366", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import collections\n\n  # Action constants\n  DOWN = 0\n  UP = 1\n  LEFT = 2\n  RIGHT = 3\n  USE = 4\n\n  # Direction mappings\n  # (dr, dc) for (DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT) actions\n  ACTION_DELTAS = {\n      DOWN: (1, 0),\n      UP: (-1, 0),\n      LEFT: (0, -1),\n      RIGHT: (0, 1),\n  }\n  # New agent direction after taking an action (CraftState dir: 0=DOWN, 1=UP, 2=LEFT, 3=RIGHT)\n  ACTION_TO_DIR = {\n      DOWN: 0,\n      UP: 1,\n      LEFT: 2,\n      RIGHT: 3\n  }\n  # Delta from agent's position to the cell it \"uses\" based on its direction\n  DIR_TO_USE_DELTA = {\n      0: (1, 0),  # If agent faces DOWN, it uses the cell one step DOWN\n      1: (-1, 0), # If agent faces UP, it uses the cell one step UP\n      2: (0, -1), # If agent faces LEFT, it uses the cell one step LEFT\n      3: (0, 1)   # If agent faces RIGHT, it uses the cell one step RIGHT\n  }\n\n  def is_traversable(r, c, grid, world_obj):\n      \"\"\"\n      Checks if a given grid cell (r, c) is traversable by the agent.\n      A cell is considered non-traversable if it's out of bounds or contains\n      any entity from the world's 'environment' set (fixed obstacles).\n      \"\"\"\n      grid_height, grid_width = grid.shape[0], grid.shape[1]\n\n      # Check bounds\n      if not (0 <= r < grid_height and 0 <= c < grid_width):\n          return False\n\n      # Check if the cell contains any \"environment\" (fixed obstacle) entity\n      # The 'environment' set in Cookbook typically contains indices of non-grabbable,\n      # fixed objects like water, unbreakable stone, workshops, etc., which act as obstacles.\n      for env_idx in world_obj.cookbook.environment:\n          if grid[r, c, env_idx] == 1:\n              return False\n      return True\n\n  # Access internal state and world from the CraftLab environment\n  # This relies on knowledge of CraftLab's internal structure for current state and world configuration.\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  world = env.world\n\n  # 1. Check if the primitive is already in the inventory\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n      return [] # Already collected, no actions needed\n\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n  start_dir = current_state.dir\n  grid_height, grid_width, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # Initialize a queue for Breadth-First Search (BFS)\n  q = collections.deque()\n  # Each item in the queue is: ((row, col, current_direction), list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state)\n  q.append(((start_pos[0], start_pos[1], start_dir), []))\n\n  # Initialize a set to keep track of visited states to avoid cycles and redundant exploration\n  # A state is defined by (row, col, current_direction)\n  visited = set()\n  visited.add((start_pos[0], start_pos[1], start_dir))\n\n  # Perform BFS\n  while q:\n      (r, c, current_dir), path = q.popleft()\n\n      # 2. Check if the current state allows immediate collection using the 'USE' action\n      # Calculate the cell that would be affected by a 'USE' action from the current position and direction\n      use_dr, use_dc = DIR_TO_USE_DELTA[current_dir]\n      target_use_r, target_use_c = r + use_dr, c + use_dc\n\n      # Check if the cell targeted by 'USE' is within grid boundaries\n      if (0 <= target_use_r < grid_height and\n          0 <= target_use_c < grid_width):\n          # Check if the target cell contains the desired primitive\n          if grid[target_use_r, target_use_c, primitive] == 1:\n              # If it does, we've found the shortest path to collect it.\n              return path + [USE]\n\n      # 3. Explore possible next move actions (DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT)\n      for action_move in [DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT]:\n          dr, dc = ACTION_DELTAS[action_move]\n          next_r, next_c = r + dr, c + dc\n          # The agent's direction changes to match the direction of the movement action taken\n          next_dir = ACTION_TO_DIR[action_move]\n\n          # Check if the next cell is traversable\n          if is_traversable(next_r, next_c, grid, world):\n              # Check if this new state (position + direction) has been visited\n              if (next_r, next_c, next_dir) not in visited:\n                  visited.add((next_r, next_c, next_dir))\n                  # Add the new state and its path to the queue\n                  q.append(((next_r, next_c, next_dir), path + [action_move]))\n\n  # If the queue becomes empty and no path was found, the primitive is unreachable\n  return []", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:15:05.170411", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    # Action constants\n    ACTION_DOWN = 0\n    ACTION_UP = 1\n    ACTION_LEFT = 2\n    ACTION_RIGHT = 3\n    ACTION_USE = 4\n\n    # Map (dy, dx) to action. Convention: (row_delta, col_delta)\n    MOVE_ACTIONS = {\n        (1, 0): ACTION_DOWN,\n        (-1, 0): ACTION_UP,\n        (0, -1): ACTION_LEFT,\n        (0, 1): ACTION_RIGHT,\n    }\n\n    # Possible (dy, dx) movements for agent\n    POSSIBLE_MOVES = [(1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)] # Down, Up, Left, Right\n\n    current_state = env._current_state\n    grid = current_state.grid\n    agent_pos = current_state.pos # (row, col)\n    inventory = current_state.inventory\n\n    # 1. Check if the primitive is already in inventory\n    if inventory[primitive] > 0:\n        return []\n\n    grid_height, grid_width, n_kinds = grid.shape\n\n    # Identify indices of entities that block movement (e.g., walls, water).\n    # These are typically the 'environment' items that are non-grabbable.\n    # The 'primitive' itself, being a resource to collect, is generally not a movement obstacle\n    # unless it's explicitly defined as a non-grabbable terrain feature.\n    obstacle_indices = env.world.non_grabbable_indices\n\n    def is_traversable(r: int, c: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if a cell (r, c) is within grid bounds and does not contain any obstacle.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Check bounds\n        if not (0 <= r < grid_height and 0 <= c < grid_width):\n            return False\n        \n        # Check if the cell contains any obstacle kind\n        # Iterate through all kinds present at (r,c) and see if any are obstacles.\n        for k_idx in range(n_kinds):\n            if grid[r, c, k_idx] > 0 and k_idx in obstacle_indices:\n                return False  # Cell contains a non-traversable obstacle\n        return True\n\n    # BFS queue: (current_position: (row, col), list_of_actions_to_reach_here)\n    q = collections.deque([(agent_pos, [])])\n    # Set of visited positions to prevent cycles and redundant exploration\n    visited = {agent_pos}\n\n    while q:\n        curr_pos, path_actions = q.popleft()\n        \n        # 2. Check if any instance of the primitive is adjacent to the current position.\n        # If so, we can perform the USE action from curr_pos to collect it.\n        for dy, dx in POSSIBLE_MOVES:\n            neighbor_r, neighbor_c = curr_pos[0] + dy, curr_pos[1] + dx\n            \n            # Check if neighbor is within bounds and contains the target primitive\n            if (0 <= neighbor_r < grid_height and 0 <= neighbor_c < grid_width) and \\\n               grid[neighbor_r, neighbor_c, primitive] > 0:\n                # Found the primitive in an adjacent cell. The path to curr_pos is `path_actions`.\n                # From curr_pos, we can execute ACTION_USE.\n                return path_actions + [ACTION_USE]\n\n        # 3. Explore further: Add valid, unvisited, and traversable neighbors to the queue.\n        for dy, dx in POSSIBLE_MOVES:\n            next_r, next_c = curr_pos[0] + dy, curr_pos[1] + dx\n            next_pos = (next_r, next_c)\n\n            if is_traversable(next_r, next_c) and next_pos not in visited:\n                visited.add(next_pos)\n                q.append((next_pos, path_actions + [MOVE_ACTIONS[(dy, dx)]]))\n    \n    # If the BFS completes and no path to an adjacent primitive is found\n    return []", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:16:42.497329", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    import numpy as np\n    # Using a list as a queue; pop(0) is inefficient for large grids but avoids 'collections' import constraint.\n\n    # Actions mapping (consistent with CraftLab.action_specs)\n    DOWN_ACTION = 0\n    UP_ACTION = 1\n    LEFT_ACTION = 2\n    RIGHT_ACTION = 3\n    USE_ACTION = 4\n\n    # Delta movements for each action (absolute grid movements)\n    _MOVES = {\n        UP_ACTION: (0, -1),   # (dx, dy) for moving upwards (decreasing y)\n        DOWN_ACTION: (0, 1),    # (dx, dy) for moving downwards (increasing y)\n        LEFT_ACTION: (-1, 0),   # (dx, dy) for moving left (decreasing x)\n        RIGHT_ACTION: (1, 0)    # (dx, dy) for moving right (increasing x)\n    }\n\n    # Reset environment to get the initial state and grid\n    obs = env.reset()\n    features_dict = obs['features_dict']\n    \n    grid = features_dict['features_global']\n    \n    # Grid dimensions (WIDTH, HEIGHT, n_kinds)\n    WIDTH, HEIGHT, _ = grid.shape\n    \n    # Convert normalized agent position to integer coordinates\n    normalized_pos = features_dict['pos']\n    initial_x = int(round(normalized_pos[0] * (WIDTH - 1)))\n    initial_y = int(round(normalized_pos[1] * (HEIGHT - 1)))\n\n    # Get indices of entities that are considered obstacles (non-grabbable environment items)\n    # env.cookbook is a CraftWorld instance, env.cookbook.environment is a set of obstacle indices.\n    obstacle_kinds = env.cookbook.environment\n\n    # BFS Initialization\n    # queue stores tuples of (current_x, current_y, path_actions_list)\n    queue = [(initial_x, initial_y, [])]\n    # visited set stores (x, y) tuples to prevent cycles and redundant exploration\n    visited = set([(initial_x, initial_y)])\n\n    # BFS Loop\n    while queue:\n        curr_x, curr_y, path = queue.pop(0) # Pop the first element (BFS)\n\n        # 1. Check if the goal (primitive) is in the 3x3 neighborhood\n        # The 'USE' action is assumed to collect an item in the 3x3 neighborhood,\n        # making the agent's direction irrelevant for collection planning.\n        for dx_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n            for dy_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                adj_x, adj_y = curr_x + dx_adj, curr_y + dy_adj\n\n                # Ensure adjacent cell is within grid bounds\n                if not (0 <= adj_x < WIDTH and 0 <= adj_y < HEIGHT):\n                    continue\n                \n                # If the target primitive is found in an adjacent cell\n                if grid[adj_x, adj_y, primitive] == 1:\n                    # We have found a path to a position from which the primitive can be collected\n                    return path + [USE_ACTION]\n\n        # 2. Explore valid neighbor cells (movement)\n        for action, (dx, dy) in _MOVES.items():\n            next_x, next_y = curr_x + dx, curr_y + dy\n\n            # Check validity of the next position\n            # a. Bounds check\n            if not (0 <= next_x < WIDTH and 0 <= next_y < HEIGHT):\n                continue\n            \n            # b. Not visited\n            if (next_x, next_y) in visited:\n                continue\n            \n            # c. Not an obstacle\n            is_obstacle = False\n            # If the next cell contains the primitive itself, we should not move into it\n            # but rather collect it from an adjacent cell.\n            if grid[next_x, next_y, primitive] == 1:\n                is_obstacle = True \n            else:\n                # Check for other predefined obstacle kinds (e.g., water, stone if non-grabbable)\n                for k_idx in obstacle_kinds:\n                    if grid[next_x, next_y, k_idx] == 1:\n                        is_obstacle = True\n                        break # Found an obstacle, no need to check further kinds for this cell\n            \n            if is_obstacle:\n                continue\n\n            # If the next position is valid, add it to the queue and visited set\n            visited.add((next_x, next_y))\n            queue.append((next_x, next_y, path + [action]))\n\n    # If the queue becomes empty and no path to collect the primitive was found\n    return []", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:16:42.569801", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    # Action constants for readability\n    DOWN = 0\n    UP = 1\n    LEFT = 2\n    RIGHT = 3\n    USE = 4\n\n    # Helper function for BFS pathfinding\n    # This helper is placed inside the function to adhere to the \"only return code within the function\" rule.\n    # In a typical module, this would likely be a separate private utility function.\n    def _bfs_path_to_targets(start_pos, targets, grid_shape):\n        q = collections.deque([(start_pos, [])]) # (current_pos_tuple, list_of_actions_to_get_here)\n        visited = {start_pos}\n        grid_h, grid_w = grid_shape\n\n        # Define movement deltas corresponding to action constants\n        # (dy, dx) for DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT\n        _MOVE_DELTAS = {\n            DOWN: (1, 0),\n            UP: (-1, 0),\n            LEFT: (0, -1),\n            RIGHT: (0, 1)\n        }\n        _ACTIONS = [DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT]\n\n        targets_set = set(targets)\n\n        while q:\n            (cy, cx), path_actions = q.popleft()\n\n            if (cy, cx) in targets_set:\n                return path_actions # Path found to one of the targets\n\n            for action in _ACTIONS:\n                dy, dx = _MOVE_DELTAS[action]\n                next_y, next_x = cy + dy, cx + dx\n                next_pos = (next_y, next_x)\n\n                # Check if the next position is within grid boundaries and has not been visited\n                if 0 <= next_y < grid_h and 0 <= next_x < grid_w and next_pos not in visited:\n                    visited.add(next_pos)\n                    q.append((next_pos, path_actions + [action]))\n        return None # No path found to any target\n\n    current_state = env._current_state # Access the internal CraftState from CraftLab\n\n    # 1. Check if the primitive is already in the inventory\n    if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n        return [] # Primitive is already collected\n\n    actions = []\n\n    # 2. Find all occurrences of the primitive in the environment grid\n    primitive_ys, primitive_xs = np.where(current_state.grid[:, :, primitive] > 0)\n\n    if len(primitive_ys) == 0:\n        # Primitive is not present in the environment\n        return []\n\n    agent_pos = current_state.pos\n    grid_h, grid_w, _ = current_state.grid.shape\n\n    # Find the closest instance of the primitive to the agent's current position\n    closest_primitive_pos = None\n    min_dist_sq = float('inf')\n    for i in range(len(primitive_ys)):\n        py, px = primitive_ys[i], primitive_xs[i]\n        dist_sq = (agent_pos[0] - py)**2 + (agent_pos[1] - px)**2\n        if dist_sq < min_dist_sq:\n            min_dist_sq = dist_sq\n            closest_primitive_pos = (py, px)\n\n    # Determine the set of valid target positions for the agent to move to\n    # in order to interact with the primitive.\n    final_targets = set()\n    py, px = closest_primitive_pos\n\n    # Interaction logic depends on whether the primitive is grabbable or non-grabbable.\n    # `env.world` refers to the `CraftWorld` instance, which holds `grabbable_indices` etc.\n    if primitive in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n        # If grabbable, the agent can move directly onto the primitive's cell to collect it.\n        final_targets.add((py, px))\n    elif primitive in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n        # If non-grabbable, the agent must be adjacent to the primitive (within its 3x3 neighborhood,\n        # excluding the primitive's own cell if it's considered un-traversable).\n        # We consider all 8 surrounding cells as potential interaction points.\n        for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n            for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                # Exclude the primitive's own cell, as it's non-grabbable\n                if dy == 0 and dx == 0:\n                    continue\n                ny, nx = py + dy, px + dx\n                # Ensure the potential target position is within grid boundaries\n                if 0 <= ny < grid_h and 0 <= nx < grid_w:\n                    final_targets.add((ny, nx))\n    else:\n        # Fallback: If the primitive is not explicitly categorized as grabbable or non-grabbable,\n        # or if it's a \"recipe output\" that behaves like a grabbable item for collection,\n        # assume it can be interacted with by moving onto its cell.\n        final_targets.add((py, px))\n    \n    # If no valid interaction targets were found (e.g., primitive is at a grid edge and all neighbors are invalid)\n    if not final_targets:\n        return []\n\n    # 3. Pathfind from the agent's current position to any of the determined target interaction positions\n    path_movement_actions = _bfs_path_to_targets(agent_pos, list(final_targets), (grid_h, grid_w))\n\n    if path_movement_actions is None:\n        return [] # No valid path could be found to any suitable interaction spot\n\n    # Add the found movement actions to the list of actions\n    actions.extend(path_movement_actions)\n\n    # 4. After moving to the interaction position, add the USE action to collect the primitive.\n    actions.append(USE)\n\n    return actions", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:18:10.668974", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  import collections\n\n  initial_state = env._current_state\n\n  # Check if the primitive is already in the inventory\n  if initial_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Initialize BFS\n  # The queue stores tuples of (CraftState object, list of actions to reach this state).\n  q = collections.deque([(initial_state, [])])\n\n  # The visited set stores a unique identifier for each state to avoid cycles and redundant work.\n  # A state is identified by its (position_tuple, direction_int, primitive_count_in_inventory).\n  # We include the primitive count to distinguish states where the primitive has been collected.\n  visited = set([(initial_state.pos, initial_state.dir, initial_state.inventory[primitive])])\n\n  # Action constants (from CraftLab.action_specs)\n  # DOWN=0, UP=1, LEFT=2, RIGHT=3, USE=4\n  movement_actions = [0, 1, 2, 3] # DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT\n  action_use = 4\n\n  # Set a maximum path length to prevent excessively long searches or infinite loops\n  MAX_PATH_LENGTH = 200 \n\n  while q:\n    current_state, path = q.popleft()\n\n    # If the current path length exceeds the maximum, stop exploring this path\n    if len(path) >= MAX_PATH_LENGTH:\n      continue\n\n    # Check if the agent is next to the primitive\n    if current_state.next_to(primitive):\n      # If next to the primitive, attempt to USE action.\n      # CraftState.step(action_use) returns a new state after applying the action.\n      _reward, state_after_use = current_state.step(action_use)\n      \n      # Check if the USE action successfully collected the primitive\n      # i.e., its count in the inventory increased in the new state.\n      if state_after_use.inventory[primitive] > current_state.inventory[primitive]:\n        return path + [action_use]\n\n    # Explore possible next states by moving\n    for action in movement_actions:\n      # Simulate the action to get the next state.\n      # CraftState.step creates a *new* CraftState object, which is essential for BFS.\n      _reward, next_state = current_state.step(action)\n      \n      # Define the identifier for the next state to check if it has been visited.\n      next_state_identifier = (next_state.pos, next_state.dir, next_state.inventory[primitive])\n\n      if next_state_identifier not in visited:\n        visited.add(next_state_identifier)\n        q.append((next_state, path + [action]))\n  \n  # If the queue becomes empty and the primitive was not collected, it's unreachable\n  # or the path exceeded MAX_PATH_LENGTH.\n  return []", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:18:11.635173", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:19:53.461081", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    actions = []\n    MAX_COLLECT_STEPS = 500  # A reasonable limit to prevent infinite loops\n\n    # Get action mappings from the environment\n    action_map = env.action_specs()\n\n    # Map agent's internal direction (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W) to the action that moves forward in that direction\n    dir_to_forward_action = {\n        0: action_map[\"UP\"],    # North -> UP action\n        1: action_map[\"RIGHT\"], # East -> RIGHT action\n        2: action_map[\"DOWN\"],  # South -> DOWN action\n        3: action_map[\"LEFT\"]   # West -> LEFT action\n    }\n\n    # State for simple stuck detection and exploration\n    last_action_was_move = False\n    stuck_count = 0\n    \n    for step_count in range(MAX_COLLECT_STEPS):\n        current_state = env._current_state # Access the underlying CraftState object\n        prev_pos = current_state.pos # Store agent's position before taking an action\n\n        # 1. Check if the primitive is already in inventory\n        if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n            break # Goal achieved, stop\n\n        # 2. Check if next to the primitive and can use it\n        if current_state.next_to(primitive):\n            # Take the USE action\n            actions.append(action_map[\"USE\"])\n            reward, done, obs = env.step(action_map[\"USE\"])\n            last_action_was_move = False # USE is not a movement action\n            stuck_count = 0 # Reset stuck counter since we're interacting with an object\n            \n            if env._current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0: # Re-check inventory after USE\n                break # Goal achieved after using\n            continue # If not collected, re-evaluate state (e.g., might need multiple uses or it was a crafting station)\n\n        # 3. If not collected and not next to, determine the next best action\n        grid = current_state.grid\n        agent_pos = current_state.pos\n        agent_dir = current_state.dir # Agent's current facing direction (0:N, 1:E, 2:S, 3:W)\n\n        # Find all locations of the primitive on the current grid\n        primitive_y_coords, primitive_x_coords = np.where(grid[:, :, primitive] > 0)\n        \n        target_pos = None\n        min_dist = float('inf')\n\n        # Find the closest primitive location using Manhattan distance\n        for py, px in zip(primitive_y_coords, primitive_x_coords):\n            dist = abs(py - agent_pos[0]) + abs(px - agent_pos[1])\n            if dist < min_dist:\n                min_dist = dist\n                target_pos = (py, px)\n\n        action_to_take = None\n\n        if target_pos: # If a primitive is found on the grid, move towards it\n            stuck_count = 0 # Reset stuck counter as we have a clear target\n            last_action_was_move = True # Assume we will take a movement action\n\n            target_y, target_x = target_pos\n            dy, dx = target_y - agent_pos[0], target_x - agent_pos[1]\n\n            desired_abs_dir = -1 # Represents the cardinal direction (N=0, E=1, S=2, W=3) to move towards\n\n            # Prioritize movement along the axis with the larger distance difference.\n            # If distances are equal, vertical movement is prioritized.\n            if abs(dy) >= abs(dx):\n                if dy < 0: desired_abs_dir = 0 # Target is North\n                elif dy > 0: desired_abs_dir = 2 # Target is South\n                else: # dy is 0, so only dx can be non-zero (target is on same row)\n                    if dx > 0: desired_abs_dir = 1 # Target is East\n                    elif dx < 0: desired_abs_dir = 3 # Target is West\n            else: # abs(dx) > abs(dy)\n                if dx > 0: desired_abs_dir = 1 # Target is East\n                elif dx < 0: desired_abs_dir = 3 # Target is West\n                else: # dx is 0, so only dy can be non-zero (target is on same column)\n                    if dy < 0: desired_abs_dir = 0 # Target is North\n                    elif dy > 0: desired_abs_dir = 2 # Target is South\n            \n            # Now, determine the action based on current facing direction and desired direction\n            if desired_abs_dir == -1: # This case implies target_pos == agent_pos (dx=0, dy=0)\n                # If agent is on the primitive, `next_to` should have caught it and triggered USE.\n                # If not, it's an edge case. Try to USE, then if still stuck, turn.\n                action_to_take = action_map[\"USE\"]\n                last_action_was_move = False # USE is not a move action\n            elif agent_dir == desired_abs_dir: # Agent is already facing the correct direction\n                action_to_take = dir_to_forward_action[agent_dir] # Move forward\n            else: # Agent needs to turn to face the desired direction\n                turn_delta = (desired_abs_dir - agent_dir + 4) % 4\n                if turn_delta == 1: # 90 degrees clockwise turn\n                    action_to_take = action_map[\"RIGHT\"]\n                elif turn_delta == 3: # 90 degrees counter-clockwise turn\n                    action_to_take = action_map[\"LEFT\"]\n                else: # turn_delta == 2 (180 degree turn)\n                    action_to_take = action_map[\"RIGHT\"] # Take one turn; next iteration will complete the 180\n                last_action_was_move = False # Turning is not a movement action\n                \n        else: # Primitive not found on the grid - explore the environment\n            # Simple exploration strategy: try to move forward in the current direction.\n            # If stuck (unable to move), try turning right to explore new areas.\n            \n            action_to_take = dir_to_forward_action[agent_dir]\n            last_action_was_move = True\n\n        # Execute the chosen action\n        actions.append(action_to_take)\n        reward, done, obs = env.step(action_to_take)\n        \n        # Stuck detection logic (only applies to movement actions)\n        if last_action_was_move:\n            new_pos = env._current_state.pos\n            if new_pos == prev_pos: # Agent did not move from its previous position\n                stuck_count += 1\n                if stuck_count >= 3: # If stuck for 3 or more consecutive \"move\" attempts\n                    # Force a turn to try a new direction, breaking out of potential local minima\n                    actions.append(action_map[\"RIGHT\"])\n                    env.step(action_map[\"RIGHT\"])\n                    stuck_count = 0 # Reset stuck counter after forcing a turn\n                    last_action_was_move = False # The forced turn is not a movement action\n            else: # Agent successfully moved\n                stuck_count = 0 # Reset stuck counter\n        else: # Action was not a move (e.g., USE, or a forced turn action)\n            stuck_count = 0 # Reset stuck counter as agent is not trying to move\n\n        if done: # If the environment signals termination for any reason\n            break\n\n    return actions", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T07:19:53.533649", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "    import collections\n\n    current_state = env._current_state\n    \n    # 1. Check if the primitive is already in inventory\n    if current_state.inventory[primitive] > 0:\n        return []\n\n    world = env.world\n    grid = current_state.grid\n    start_pos = current_state.pos\n    WIDTH, HEIGHT, N_KINDS = grid.shape\n\n    # Get action integer values from the environment's specs\n    actions_map = env.action_specs()\n    ACTION_DOWN = actions_map['DOWN']\n    ACTION_UP = actions_map['UP']\n    ACTION_LEFT = actions_map['LEFT']\n    ACTION_RIGHT = actions_map['RIGHT']\n    ACTION_USE = actions_map['USE']\n\n    # Define move deltas for BFS exploration\n    MOVE_DELTAS = {\n        ACTION_UP: (0, -1),   # (dx, dy) for moving North\n        ACTION_DOWN: (0, 1),  # (dx, dy) for moving South\n        ACTION_LEFT: (-1, 0), # (dx, dy) for moving West\n        ACTION_RIGHT: (1, 0), # (dx, dy) for moving East\n    }\n\n    # Identify non-walkable terrain (water and stone)\n    # Check if these indices are actually defined in the world\n    water_idx = world.water_index if hasattr(world, 'water_index') else -1\n    stone_idx = world.stone_index if hasattr(world, 'stone_index') else -1\n\n    # 2. Find all locations of the primitive on the grid\n    primitive_locations = []\n    for x in range(WIDTH):\n        for y in range(HEIGHT):\n            if grid[x, y, primitive] == 1:\n                primitive_locations.append((x, y))\n\n    if not primitive_locations:\n        return []  # Primitive not found on the grid\n\n    # 3. Perform BFS to find the shortest path to a cell adjacent to the primitive\n    queue = collections.deque([(start_pos[0], start_pos[1], [])])  # (x, y, path_actions)\n    visited = set([(start_pos[0], start_pos[1])])\n\n    while queue:\n        x, y, path = queue.popleft()\n\n        # Check if the current cell (x, y) is adjacent to any primitive location\n        # If it is, we are ready to 'USE' the primitive\n        for px, py in primitive_locations:\n            if abs(x - px) + abs(y - py) == 1: # Manhattan distance of 1 means adjacent\n                # Found the shortest path to an adjacent cell. Append USE action.\n                return path + [ACTION_USE]\n\n        # Explore neighbors\n        for action, (dx, dy) in MOVE_DELTAS.items():\n            nx, ny = x + dx, y + dy\n\n            # Check bounds\n            if 0 <= nx < WIDTH and 0 <= ny < HEIGHT:\n                # Check for obstacles (water, stone)\n                is_obstacle = False\n                if water_idx != -1 and grid[nx, ny, water_idx] == 1:\n                    is_obstacle = True\n                if stone_idx != -1 and grid[nx, ny, stone_idx] == 1:\n                    is_obstacle = True\n\n                if not is_obstacle and (nx, ny) not in visited:\n                    visited.add((nx, ny))\n                    queue.append((nx, ny, path + [action]))\n\n    # If BFS completes and no path to an adjacent primitive is found\n    return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
